0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:50,650
Bloody kids.

2
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:40,760
How fastidious you've become,Wormtail.

3
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:45,340
As I recall, you once calledthe nearest gutter pipe home.

4
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:50,710
Could it be that the task of nursing mehas become wearisome for you?

5
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,350
Oh, no. No, no, my Lord Voldemort.

6
00:02:53,550 --> 00:02:54,780
I only meant...

7
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:57,920
...perhaps if we were to do itwithout the boy.

8
00:02:58,090 --> 00:03:00,490
No! The boy is everything!

9
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:04,180
It cannot be done without him.And it will be done.

10
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:07,020
Exactly as I said.

11
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:11,130
-I will not disappoint you, my Lord.-Good.

12
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,360
First, gather our old comrades.

13
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:16,770
Send them a sign.

14
00:03:28,490 --> 00:03:31,980
Nagini tells methe old Muggle caretaker...

15
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:35,850
...is standing just outside the door.

16
00:03:36,030 --> 00:03:41,330
Step aside, Wormtail,so I can give our guest a proper greeting.

17
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,330
Avada Kedavra!

18
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:49,860
Harry.

19
00:03:50,610 --> 00:03:52,270
Harry!

20
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:55,370
Are you all right?

21
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:58,170
Hermione. Bad dream.

22
00:03:58,350 --> 00:04:01,720
-When did you get here?-Just now. You?

23
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:03,110
Last night.

24
00:04:03,290 --> 00:04:05,520
Wake up! Wake up, Ronald!

25
00:04:05,690 --> 00:04:06,950
Bloody hell.

26
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,650
Honestly, get dressed.

27
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:11,120
And don't go back to sleep.

28
00:04:11,290 --> 00:04:14,630
Come on, Ron!Your mother says breakfast's ready!

29
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,140
-Ron, where are we actually going?-Don't know.

30
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:27,870
-Hey, Dad. Where are we going?-Haven't the foggiest.

31
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,570
Keep up!

32
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:33,980
Arthur!

33
00:04:34,150 --> 00:04:36,140
It's about time, son.

34
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:40,690
Sorry, Amos. Some of ushad a bit of a sleepy start.

35
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:46,520
This is Amos Diggory, everyone.Works with me at the Ministry.

36
00:04:46,730 --> 00:04:49,220
And this strapping young ladmust be Cedric, am I right?

37
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,560
Yes, sir.

38
00:04:50,730 --> 00:04:52,400
This way.

39
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:57,500
Merlin's beard!You must be Harry Potter.

40
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,400
-Yes, sir.-Great, great pleasure.

41
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:02,370
Pleasure to meet you too, sir.

42
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:07,680
Yes, it's just over there.

43
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:11,750
-Shall we?-Oh, yeah.

44
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,120
We don't want to be late.

45
00:05:13,290 --> 00:05:17,420
Come on. Nearly there now.Get yourself into a good position.

46
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:20,760
Why are they all standing aroundthat manky old boot?

47
00:05:20,930 --> 00:05:23,420
-That isn't just any manky old boot.-It's a Portkey.

48
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,970
Time to go!

49
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,730
What's a Portkey?

50
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:30,930
-Ready! After three. One, two...-Harry!

51
00:05:31,110 --> 00:05:32,200
...three!

52
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:44,380
Let go, kids!

53
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:47,150
-What?!-Let go!

54
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,760
I'll bet that cleared your sinuses, eh?

55
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:05,310
-Total shambles, as per usual.-Thanks.

56
00:06:11,110 --> 00:06:13,240
Go on, look at that!

57
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:18,010
Well, kids, welcome tothe Quidditch World Cup!

58
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:23,650
Stay together! Keep up, girls!

59
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,460
Look!

60
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,630
Come on! Keep up, girls!

61
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:37,940
Blimey!

62
00:06:38,110 --> 00:06:39,970
Parting of the ways, I think, old chap.

63
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:41,540
-See you at the match.-See you.

64
00:06:41,710 --> 00:06:43,010
-Cedric.-Ced, come on.

65
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,870
See you later, Cedric.

66
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:51,580
Home sweet home.

67
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:54,910
What?

68
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:04,230
-Excellent, excellent.-Ginny, look!

69
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,700
-All to the bath.-Look.

70
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:08,360
Girls, choose a bunk and unpack.

71
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,410
Ron, get out of the kitchen.We're all hungry.

72
00:07:11,570 --> 00:07:14,040
-Yeah, get out of the kitchen, Ron!-Feet off the table!

73
00:07:14,210 --> 00:07:16,470
-Feet off the table!-Feet off the table!

74
00:07:17,710 --> 00:07:19,910
I love magic.

75
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:38,660
Get your Quidditch World Cupprograms here!

76
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:42,070
Blimey, Dad. How far up are we?

77
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,670
Well, put it this way:

78
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:45,640
If it rains...

79
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:48,180
...you'll be the first to know.

80
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:51,310
Father and I are inthe minister's box...

81
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:54,750
...by personal invitationof Cornelius Fudge himself.

82
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:57,110
Don't boast, Draco.

83
00:07:57,290 --> 00:07:59,380
There's no need with these people.

84
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,380
Do enjoy yourself, won't you?

85
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,590
While you can.

86
00:08:20,010 --> 00:08:24,670
Come on up. Take your seats. I told youthese seats would be worth waiting for.

87
00:08:24,850 --> 00:08:26,710
Come on!

88
00:08:28,950 --> 00:08:30,920
It's the lrish! There's Troy!

89
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:32,920
-And Mullet!-And Moran!

90
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,500
Ireland! Ireland! Ireland!

91
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:48,930
-Here come the Bulgarians!-Yes!

92
00:08:55,010 --> 00:08:56,380
Who's that?

93
00:08:57,110 --> 00:09:00,170
That, sis, is the best Seekerin the world.

94
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:05,750
Krum! Krum! Krum!

95
00:09:10,490 --> 00:09:11,720
Krum!

96
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:13,620
Yes!

97
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:23,270
Good evening!

98
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:26,800
As Minister for Magic...

99
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:30,070
...it gives me great pleasure...

100
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:34,450
...to welcomeeach and every one of you...

101
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:40,490
...to the finalof the 422nd Quidditch World Cup!

102
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,490
Let the match...

103
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:44,450
...begin!

104
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,760
Krum! Krum! Krum!

105
00:10:00,610 --> 00:10:02,270
There's no one like Krum.

106
00:10:02,450 --> 00:10:04,040
-Krum?-Dumb Krum?

107
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:07,270
He's like a bird,the way he rides the wind.

108
00:10:07,450 --> 00:10:10,350
-He's more than an athlete.-Dumb Krum.

109
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,920
He's an artist.

110
00:10:12,090 --> 00:10:14,350
-I think you're in love, Ron.-Shut up.

111
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,920
Viktor, I love you

112
00:10:16,090 --> 00:10:17,680
Viktor, I do

113
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:21,090
When we're apartMy heart beats only for you

114
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:23,930
Sounds like the lrishhave got their pride on.

115
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,830
Stop! Stop it!

116
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:27,960
It's not the lrish.

117
00:10:29,110 --> 00:10:31,270
We've gotta get out of here. Now!

118
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:35,740
Get out, it's the Death Eaters!

119
00:10:35,910 --> 00:10:39,280
Get back to the Portkey, everybody,and stick together!

120
00:10:39,450 --> 00:10:42,110
Fred, George!Ginny is your responsibility.

121
00:10:42,650 --> 00:10:44,420
Go!

122
00:10:44,590 --> 00:10:46,420
Harry!

123
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,400
-Keep up, you lot!-Harry!

124
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:06,800
Harry! Harry!

125
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:55,950
Morsmordre!

126
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,210
Harry!

127
00:12:25,690 --> 00:12:28,920
-Where are you?-Harry!

128
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,790
We've been looking for you for ages!

129
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,730
Thought we lost you, mate.

130
00:12:36,530 --> 00:12:38,520
What is that?

131
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,700
Stupefy!

132
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:45,200
Stop!

133
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:47,610
That's my son!

134
00:12:48,650 --> 00:12:51,310
-Ron, Harry, Hermione, you all right?-We came back for Harry.

135
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,780
Which of you conjured it?

136
00:12:52,950 --> 00:12:55,110
-Crouch, you can't possi---Do not lie!

137
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,280
You've been discoveredat the scene of the crime.

138
00:12:57,450 --> 00:12:59,480
-Crime?-Barty! They're just kids.

139
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:01,150
What crime?

140
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,820
It's the Dark Mark, Harry. It's his mark.

141
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:05,150
What, Voldemort?

142
00:13:06,330 --> 00:13:10,200
Those people tonight, in the masks,they're his too, aren't they?

143
00:13:10,370 --> 00:13:12,600
-His followers?-Yeah.

144
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,670
Death Eaters.

145
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:19,430
-Follow me.-There was a man, before.

146
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:21,270
There!

147
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:23,740
All of you, this way!

148
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,910
A man, Harry?

149
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:27,680
Who?

150
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,880
I don't know.

151
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,720
I didn't see his face.

152
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:51,960
Anything from the trolley?

153
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:57,210
Anything from the trolley?

154
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:02,880
Anything from the trolley, dears?

155
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:05,250
Packet of Drooble's...

156
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:07,220
...and a Licorice Wand.

157
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:10,750
On second thought, just the Drooble's.

158
00:14:10,930 --> 00:14:14,920
-It's all right, I'll get it. Don't worry.-Just the Drooble's. Thanks.

159
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:18,600
Two Pumpkin Pasties, please.

160
00:14:23,970 --> 00:14:25,600
Thank you.

161
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,440
Anything sweet for you, dear?

162
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,610
Oh, no, I'm not hungry. Thank you.

163
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,540
Anything from the trolley?

164
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,740
This is horrible.

165
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:39,850
How can the Ministrynot know who conjured it?

166
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:41,790
Wasn't there any security or...?

167
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:44,760
Loads, according to Dad.

168
00:14:44,930 --> 00:14:48,890
That's what worried them so much.Happened right under their noses.

169
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,940
It's hurting again, isn't it? Your scar.

170
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:56,770
I'm fine.

171
00:14:58,810 --> 00:15:01,710
You know Sirius willwant to hear about this...

172
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:05,840
...what you saw at the World Cupand the dream.

173
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:17,490
Hedwig. There we go.

174
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:58,960
Clear the runway!

175
00:16:04,370 --> 00:16:07,140
Well, there's somethingyou don't see every day.

176
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:36,040
Well, now we're all settled in and sorted,I'd like to make an announcement.

177
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:40,440
This castle will not only beyour home this year...

178
00:16:40,610 --> 00:16:43,770
...but home to somevery special guests as well.

179
00:16:44,150 --> 00:16:46,770
You see, Hogwarts has been chosen....

180
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,210
Yes, what is it?

181
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,780
What is it?

182
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:56,460
Tell them to wait.Tell them to wait. Wait.

183
00:16:56,660 --> 00:17:02,600
So Hogwarts has been chosento host a legendary event:

184
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:04,820
The Triwizard Tournament.

185
00:17:05,370 --> 00:17:07,430
-For those of you who do not know...-Brilliant.

186
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,770
...the Triwizard Tournamentbrings together three schools...

187
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:13,070
...for a series of magical contests.

188
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:16,770
From each school, a single studentis selected to compete.

189
00:17:16,950 --> 00:17:18,640
Now let me be clear.

190
00:17:18,810 --> 00:17:21,750
If chosen, you stand alone.

191
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,850
And trust me when I say...

192
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:26,990
...these contests are notfor the faint-hearted.

193
00:17:27,290 --> 00:17:31,620
But more of that later.For now, please join me in welcoming...

194
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:35,820
...the lovely ladies of theBeauxbatons Academy of Magic...

195
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,990
...and their headmistress,Madame Maxime.

196
00:17:52,550 --> 00:17:54,110
Bloody hell.

197
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:04,290
Blimey. That's one big woman.

198
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,370
And now our friends from the north.

199
00:18:28,550 --> 00:18:31,380
Please greet the proud sonsof Durmstrang...

200
00:18:31,550 --> 00:18:34,390
...and their high master,lgor Karkaroff.

201
00:18:57,450 --> 00:18:59,000
Oh, it's Krum!

202
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,650
Blimey, it's him!

203
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:02,680
Viktor Krum!

204
00:19:11,590 --> 00:19:13,030
Albus.

205
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,920
Igor.

206
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:32,210
Professor Dumbly-dorr,my horses have traveled a long way.

207
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,910
-They will need attending to.-Don't worry, Madame Maxime.

208
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:38,610
Our gamekeeper, Hagrid,is more than capable of seeing to them.

209
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:41,050
But you know, Monsieur Hagrid...

210
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,920
...they drink only single-malt whiskey.

211
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:51,830
You idiot!

212
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:58,830
Your attention, please!

213
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:03,340
I'd like to say a few words.

214
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:07,140
Eternal glory.

215
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:11,610
That is what awaits the studentwho wins the Triwizard Tournament.

216
00:20:11,790 --> 00:20:15,990
But to do this, that studentmust survive three tasks.

217
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:20,120
Three extremely dangerous tasks.

218
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:21,550
-Wicked.-Wicked.

219
00:20:21,730 --> 00:20:25,960
For this reason, the Ministry has seen fitto impose a new rule.

220
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,500
To explain all this...

221
00:20:27,670 --> 00:20:31,300
...we have the head of the Departmentof lnternational Magical Cooperation...

222
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:33,640
...Mr. Bartemius Crouch.

223
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:50,790
Bloody hell. It's Mad-Eye Moody.

224
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:54,760
-Alastor Moody? The Auror?-Auror?

225
00:20:54,930 --> 00:20:58,390
Dark-wizard catcher. Half the cellsin Azkaban are filled thanks to him.

226
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,200
He's supposed to be mad as a hatter,though, these days.

227
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:17,750
-My dear old friend, thanks for coming.-Stupid ceiling.

228
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,010
Thank you.

229
00:21:25,530 --> 00:21:27,390
What's that he's drinking,do you suppose?

230
00:21:27,830 --> 00:21:30,820
I don't know, but I don't thinkit's pumpkin juice.

231
00:21:37,810 --> 00:21:39,740
After due consideration...

232
00:21:39,910 --> 00:21:42,810
...the Ministry has concluded that,for their own safety...

233
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:45,950
...no student under the age of 1 7...

234
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:49,850
...shall be allowed to put forth theirname for the Triwizard Tournament.

235
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:52,720
-This decision is final.-That's rubbish!

236
00:21:52,890 --> 00:21:55,480
That's rubbish!You don't know what you're doing!

237
00:21:55,660 --> 00:21:59,390
-Silence!-They're not too happy about that, then.

238
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:21,220
The Goblet of Fire.

239
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:24,690
Anyone wishing to submit themselvesto the tournament...

240
00:22:24,850 --> 00:22:27,750
...need only write their nameupon a piece of parchment...

241
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:31,020
...and throw it in the flame beforethis hour on Thursday night.

242
00:22:32,130 --> 00:22:34,360
Do not do so lightly.

243
00:22:34,730 --> 00:22:38,290
If chosen, there's no turning back.

244
00:22:38,470 --> 00:22:43,430
As from this moment,the Triwizard Tournament has begun.

245
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:11,660
Alastor Moody.

246
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,230
Ex-Auror...

247
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:19,370
...Ministry malcontent...

248
00:23:19,580 --> 00:23:21,980
...and your newDefense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

249
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:26,600
I am here because Dumbledore asked me.End of story, goodbye, the end.

250
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:28,550
Any questions?

251
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,450
When it comes to the Dark Arts...

252
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:37,490
...I believe in a practical approach.

253
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:43,360
But first, which of you can tell mehow many Unforgivable Curses there are?

254
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:46,230
-Three, sir.-And they are so named?

255
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:49,630
Because they are unforgivable.The use of any one of them will--

256
00:23:49,810 --> 00:23:53,940
Will earn you a one-way ticketto Azkaban, correct.

257
00:23:54,110 --> 00:23:56,840
The Ministry says you're too youngto see what these curses do.

258
00:23:57,010 --> 00:24:00,470
I say different! You need to knowwhat you're up against!

259
00:24:00,650 --> 00:24:02,810
You need to be prepared.

260
00:24:02,990 --> 00:24:05,450
You need to find another placeto put your chewing gum...

261
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:07,920
...besides the underside of your desk,Mr. Finnigan!

262
00:24:08,090 --> 00:24:11,080
No way. The old codgercan see out the back of his head.

263
00:24:11,790 --> 00:24:13,560
And hear across classrooms!

264
00:24:15,900 --> 00:24:19,390
So which curse shall we see first?

265
00:24:19,570 --> 00:24:20,800
-Weasley!-Yes?

266
00:24:20,970 --> 00:24:22,300
Stand.

267
00:24:25,470 --> 00:24:27,240
Give us a curse.

268
00:24:27,410 --> 00:24:31,280
Well, my dad did tell me about one.

269
00:24:31,850 --> 00:24:33,110
The lmperius Curse.

270
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:36,580
Oh, yeah, your fatherwould know all about that.

271
00:24:36,990 --> 00:24:39,650
Gave the Ministry quite a bit of griefa few years ago.

272
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:42,610
Perhaps this will show you why.

273
00:24:50,230 --> 00:24:51,560
Hello.

274
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,900
Lovely little beauty.

275
00:24:58,040 --> 00:25:00,030
Engorgio.

276
00:25:00,410 --> 00:25:02,070
Imperio!

277
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:08,920
Don't worry. It's completely harmless.

278
00:25:15,090 --> 00:25:16,750
If she bites...

279
00:25:17,290 --> 00:25:18,780
...she's lethal.

280
00:25:21,330 --> 00:25:23,130
What are you laughing at?

281
00:25:24,470 --> 00:25:25,900
Get off!

282
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:30,100
Talented, isn't she?

283
00:25:30,270 --> 00:25:33,670
What should I have her do next?Jump out the window?

284
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:37,040
Drown herself?

285
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:52,090
Scores of witches and wizardshave claimed...

286
00:25:52,260 --> 00:25:56,250
...that they only didYou-Know-Who's bidding...

287
00:25:56,430 --> 00:25:58,660
...under the influenceof the lmperius Curse.

288
00:25:58,830 --> 00:26:00,770
But here's the rub:

289
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:04,100
How do we sort out the liars?

290
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:08,140
Another, another.

291
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:10,670
Up, up. Come on.

292
00:26:10,850 --> 00:26:12,400
Longbottom, is it?

293
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:14,570
Up.

294
00:26:16,620 --> 00:26:20,490
Professor Sprout tells meyou have an aptitude for herbology.

295
00:26:22,390 --> 00:26:24,020
There's the....

296
00:26:24,260 --> 00:26:26,190
The Cruciatus Curse.

297
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:29,230
Correct, correct. Come, come.

298
00:26:29,430 --> 00:26:31,060
Particularly nasty.

299
00:26:34,100 --> 00:26:35,930
The torture curse.

300
00:26:36,940 --> 00:26:39,100
Crucio!

301
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:55,620
Stop it! Can't you seeit's bothering him? Stop it!

302
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:17,240
Perhaps you could give us the lastUnforgivable Curse, Miss Granger.

303
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,010
No?

304
00:27:22,220 --> 00:27:24,340
Avada Kedavra!

305
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:29,650
The Killing Curse.

306
00:27:30,790 --> 00:27:33,920
Only one person is knownto have survived it...

307
00:27:34,500 --> 00:27:36,860
...and he's sitting in this room.

308
00:28:08,460 --> 00:28:10,230
Brilliant, isn't he?

309
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:14,430
Completely demented, of course, andterrifying to be in the same room with...

310
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:17,770
...but he's really been there, you know?He's looked evil in the eye.

311
00:28:17,940 --> 00:28:20,530
There's a reason those cursesare unforgivable.

312
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:24,810
To perform them in a classroom....I mean, did you see Neville's face?

313
00:28:27,750 --> 00:28:29,220
Neville?

314
00:28:29,380 --> 00:28:30,820
Son?

315
00:28:31,190 --> 00:28:32,810
You all right?

316
00:28:33,790 --> 00:28:37,160
Come on. We'll have a cup of tea.I want to show you something.

317
00:28:51,710 --> 00:28:53,700
We're gonna be late!

318
00:29:07,290 --> 00:29:09,620
Come on, Cedric. Put it in!

319
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:27,730
Eternal glory. Be brilliant, wouldn't it?

320
00:29:27,910 --> 00:29:30,540
Three years from now,when we're old enough to be chosen.

321
00:29:30,710 --> 00:29:32,340
Yeah, rather you than me.

322
00:29:32,510 --> 00:29:34,450
Yes!

323
00:29:36,650 --> 00:29:38,550
Thank you, thank you.

324
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:41,780
-Well, lads, we've done it.-Cooked it up just this morning.

325
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:44,120
It's not going to work.

326
00:29:45,330 --> 00:29:47,820
-Oh, yeah?-And why is that, Granger?

327
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:50,970
You see this? This is an Age Line.

328
00:29:51,130 --> 00:29:52,930
Dumbledore drew it himself.

329
00:29:53,100 --> 00:29:54,530
So?

330
00:29:56,140 --> 00:29:59,730
So a genius like Dumbledorecouldn't possibly be fooled...

331
00:29:59,910 --> 00:30:02,900
...by a dodge as pathetically dimwittedas an Aging Potion.

332
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:07,340
-But that's why it's so brilliant.-Because it's so pathetically dimwitted.

333
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:11,080
-Ready, Fred?-Ready, George.

334
00:30:11,250 --> 00:30:13,080
-Bottoms up.-Bottoms up.

335
00:30:16,530 --> 00:30:18,430
-Yes!-Yes!

336
00:30:19,290 --> 00:30:20,760
Yeah!

337
00:30:21,930 --> 00:30:23,560
Yes!

338
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:25,490
Ready?

339
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:30,930
-Yes!-Yes!

340
00:30:39,480 --> 00:30:41,450
-You said!-You said!

341
00:30:42,420 --> 00:30:45,850
-Oh, right, you want a piece of me?!-I'll tear your ears off!

342
00:30:46,020 --> 00:30:48,510
-Now you're making me laugh.-Take this! Come on!

343
00:30:48,690 --> 00:30:50,120
Fight! Fight! Fight!

344
00:30:55,230 --> 00:30:56,960
We're "old school," right?

345
00:30:57,130 --> 00:30:59,530
Yeah, but you look older!

346
00:31:30,900 --> 00:31:33,560
Sit down. Please.

347
00:31:36,970 --> 00:31:39,840
Now the momentyou've all been waiting for:

348
00:31:40,010 --> 00:31:42,140
The champion selection.

349
00:32:13,580 --> 00:32:17,380
The Durmstrang championis Viktor Krum.

350
00:32:33,330 --> 00:32:35,730
The champion for Beauxbatons...

351
00:32:35,900 --> 00:32:37,920
...is Fleur Delacour.

352
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:51,470
The Hogwarts champion, Cedric Diggory!

353
00:33:01,520 --> 00:33:05,930
Excellent! We now haveour three champions.

354
00:33:06,090 --> 00:33:10,290
But in the end,only one will go down in history.

355
00:33:10,470 --> 00:33:13,800
Only one will hoistthis chalice of champions...

356
00:33:14,100 --> 00:33:17,130
...this vessel of victory...

357
00:33:17,310 --> 00:33:19,500
...the Triwizard Cup!

358
00:33:50,270 --> 00:33:51,930
Harry Potter.

359
00:33:54,040 --> 00:33:55,670
Harry Potter?

360
00:34:00,050 --> 00:34:02,240
No. No.

361
00:34:02,750 --> 00:34:04,050
Harry Potter!

362
00:34:04,490 --> 00:34:05,980
Go on, Harry.

363
00:34:06,150 --> 00:34:07,920
Harry, for goodness sake.

364
00:34:39,420 --> 00:34:40,620
He's a cheat!

365
00:34:41,160 --> 00:34:43,720
He's not even 1 7 yet!

366
00:35:11,590 --> 00:35:15,080
-It's wrong, I tell you!-You French tart.

367
00:35:15,260 --> 00:35:18,230
-Everything is a conspiracy theory with you!-Quiet! I can't think!

368
00:35:18,390 --> 00:35:20,380
-Everything is a conspiracy theory!-I protest.

369
00:35:20,560 --> 00:35:21,760
-Harry.-I protest!

370
00:35:21,930 --> 00:35:23,800
Did you put your namein the Goblet of Fire?

371
00:35:23,970 --> 00:35:26,130
-No, sir.-Did you ask one of the older students...

372
00:35:26,300 --> 00:35:27,630
-...to do it for you?-No, sir.

373
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:30,700
-You're absolutely sure?-Yes. Yes, sir.

374
00:35:31,140 --> 00:35:33,370
-But of course he is lying.-The hell he is!

375
00:35:33,580 --> 00:35:35,940
The Goblet of Fire is an exceptionallypowerful magical object.

376
00:35:36,110 --> 00:35:39,240
Only an exceptionally powerfulConfundus Charm could have hoodwinked it.

377
00:35:39,410 --> 00:35:41,410
Magic way beyond the talentsof a fourth year.

378
00:35:41,580 --> 00:35:44,580
You seem to have given thisa fair bit of thought, Mad-Eye.

379
00:35:44,750 --> 00:35:47,920
It was once my job to thinkas dark wizards do, Karkaroff...

380
00:35:48,090 --> 00:35:51,180
-...perhaps you remember.-This doesn't help, Alastor.

381
00:35:52,960 --> 00:35:55,260
Leave this to you, Barty.

382
00:35:56,630 --> 00:35:58,830
The rules are absolute.

383
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:03,770
The Goblet of Fire constitutesa binding magical contract.

384
00:36:05,310 --> 00:36:07,500
Mr. Potter has no choice.

385
00:36:08,310 --> 00:36:10,640
He is, as of tonight...

386
00:36:12,450 --> 00:36:14,470
...a Triwizard champion.

387
00:36:42,410 --> 00:36:44,540
This can't go on, Albus.

388
00:36:44,880 --> 00:36:47,710
First the Dark Mark. Now this?

389
00:36:47,880 --> 00:36:49,870
What do you suggest, Minerva?

390
00:36:51,050 --> 00:36:53,110
Put an end to it.

391
00:36:53,590 --> 00:36:55,580
Don't let Potter compete.

392
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:58,230
You heard Barty. The rules are clear.

393
00:36:58,390 --> 00:37:01,230
Well, the devil with Bartyand his rules.

394
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:03,830
And since when did youaccommodate the Ministry?

395
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:07,990
Headmaster, l, too, find it difficultto believe this mere coincidence.

396
00:37:08,170 --> 00:37:12,110
However, if we are to truly discoverthe meaning of these events...

397
00:37:12,270 --> 00:37:15,870
...perhaps we should,for the time being...

398
00:37:16,780 --> 00:37:19,040
...Iet them unfold.

399
00:37:19,210 --> 00:37:21,380
What--? Do nothing?

400
00:37:21,550 --> 00:37:23,180
Offer him up as bait?

401
00:37:24,190 --> 00:37:27,020
Potter is a boy, not a piece of meat.

402
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:30,650
I agree. With Severus.

403
00:37:31,230 --> 00:37:34,060
Alastor, keep an eye on Harry, will you?

404
00:37:34,330 --> 00:37:36,800
-I can do that.-Don't let him know, though.

405
00:37:37,070 --> 00:37:40,160
He must be anxious enough as it is...

406
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:43,360
...knowing what lies ahead.

407
00:37:43,740 --> 00:37:46,300
Then again, we all are.

408
00:38:01,190 --> 00:38:02,990
How did you do it?

409
00:38:04,460 --> 00:38:09,090
Never mind. Doesn't matter.Might've let your best friend know, though.

410
00:38:09,260 --> 00:38:12,560
-Let you know what?-You know bloody well what.

411
00:38:12,730 --> 00:38:15,130
I didn't ask for this to happen, Ron.

412
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:17,200
Okay?

413
00:38:17,370 --> 00:38:19,860
-You're being stupid.-Yeah, that's me.

414
00:38:20,040 --> 00:38:23,570
Ron Weasley,Harry Potter's stupid friend.

415
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:29,250
I didn't put my name in that cup.

416
00:38:29,680 --> 00:38:33,520
I don't want eternal glory.I just wanna be....

417
00:38:35,290 --> 00:38:39,750
Look, I don't know what happened tonight,and I don't know why.

418
00:38:39,930 --> 00:38:41,160
It just did.

419
00:38:42,030 --> 00:38:43,590
Okay?

420
00:38:52,410 --> 00:38:54,170
Piss off.

421
00:39:09,190 --> 00:39:11,660
What a charismatic quartet.

422
00:39:12,990 --> 00:39:14,590
Hello.

423
00:39:15,460 --> 00:39:18,020
I'm Rita Skeeter.

424
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:21,090
I write for the Daily Prophet.

425
00:39:21,700 --> 00:39:26,400
But of course you know that, don't you?It's you we don't know.

426
00:39:26,940 --> 00:39:28,770
You're the juicy news.

427
00:39:28,940 --> 00:39:33,140
What quirks lurkbeneath those rosy cheeks?

428
00:39:33,350 --> 00:39:36,810
What mysteries do the muscles mask?

429
00:39:36,990 --> 00:39:40,220
Does courage lie beneath those curls?

430
00:39:40,390 --> 00:39:43,410
In short, what makes a champion tick?

431
00:39:43,930 --> 00:39:48,230
" Me, Myself & l" want to know.Not to mention my rabid readers.

432
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:50,890
So who's feeling up to sharing?

433
00:39:54,200 --> 00:39:56,800
Shall we start with the youngest?Lovely.

434
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:10,880
This is cozy.

435
00:40:11,450 --> 00:40:13,150
It's a broom cupboard.

436
00:40:13,520 --> 00:40:15,820
You should feel right at home, then.

437
00:40:16,020 --> 00:40:18,790
Don't mind if I usea Quick-Quotes Quill, do you?

438
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:20,520
No.

439
00:40:20,900 --> 00:40:22,890
So tell me, Harry.

440
00:40:23,060 --> 00:40:25,970
Here you sit, a mere boy of 1 2--

441
00:40:26,130 --> 00:40:27,620
I'm 1 4. Sorry.

442
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:30,770
--about to competeagainst three students...

443
00:40:30,940 --> 00:40:34,200
...not only vastly moreemotionally mature than yourself...

444
00:40:34,380 --> 00:40:36,970
...but who have mastered spellsthat you wouldn't attempt...

445
00:40:37,150 --> 00:40:39,480
...in your dizziest daydreams.

446
00:40:39,980 --> 00:40:42,010
Concerned?

447
00:40:43,180 --> 00:40:46,020
I don't know.I haven't really thought about it.

448
00:40:46,190 --> 00:40:48,050
Just ignore the quill.

449
00:40:48,520 --> 00:40:51,050
Then, of course,you're no ordinary boy of 1 2, are you?

450
00:40:51,230 --> 00:40:53,820
-Fourteen.-Your story's legend.

451
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:56,760
Do you think it wasthe trauma of your past...

452
00:40:56,930 --> 00:41:00,160
...that made you so keen to entersuch a dangerous tournament?

453
00:41:00,340 --> 00:41:02,100
No, I didn't enter.

454
00:41:02,270 --> 00:41:03,860
Of course you didn't.

455
00:41:06,140 --> 00:41:07,770
Everyone loves a rebel, Harry.

456
00:41:10,080 --> 00:41:11,600
Scratch that last.

457
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:16,540
Speaking of your parents, were they alive,how do you think they'd feel?

458
00:41:16,720 --> 00:41:18,520
Proud? Or concerned...

459
00:41:18,690 --> 00:41:22,520
...that your attitude shows, at best,a pathological need for attention...

460
00:41:22,690 --> 00:41:25,280
...at worst, a psychotic death wish?

461
00:41:26,290 --> 00:41:31,360
Hey, my eyes aren't"glistening with the ghosts of my past."

462
00:42:03,660 --> 00:42:06,000
Harry, I couldn 't risk sending Hedwig.

463
00:42:06,170 --> 00:42:09,430
Since the World Cup, the Ministry'sbeen intercepting more and more owls...

464
00:42:09,600 --> 00:42:11,830
...and she 's too easily recognized.

465
00:42:12,010 --> 00:42:14,870
We need to talk, Harry, face-to-face.

466
00:42:15,040 --> 00:42:19,210
Meet me in the Gryffindor common room,1 :00 this Saturday night.

467
00:42:19,380 --> 00:42:21,140
And make sure you 're alone.

468
00:42:21,320 --> 00:42:22,810
Sirius.

469
00:42:22,980 --> 00:42:24,470
P. S.:

470
00:42:24,650 --> 00:42:26,450
The bird bites.

471
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:38,230
Sirius?

472
00:42:55,120 --> 00:42:57,020
Harry Potter, age 1 2...

473
00:42:57,190 --> 00:43:00,150
...suspect entrantin the Triwizard Tournament.

474
00:43:00,320 --> 00:43:02,920
His eyes swimmingwith the ghosts of his past...

475
00:43:03,090 --> 00:43:04,650
...and choking back tears....

476
00:43:20,140 --> 00:43:22,740
Sirius. How--?

477
00:43:22,910 --> 00:43:25,400
I don ' t have much time,so let me get straight to it.

478
00:43:25,580 --> 00:43:28,520
Did you or did you not put your nameinto the Goblet of Fire?

479
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:30,150
No!

480
00:43:30,750 --> 00:43:32,010
I had to ask.

481
00:43:32,190 --> 00:43:36,990
Now, tell me about this dream of yours.You mentioned Wormtail and Voldemort.

482
00:43:37,160 --> 00:43:39,590
But who was the third man in the room?

483
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:42,250
-I don't know.-You didn't hear a name?

484
00:43:43,100 --> 00:43:44,620
No.

485
00:43:45,530 --> 00:43:49,260
Voldemort was giving him a job to do.Something important.

486
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:50,730
And what was that?

487
00:43:52,910 --> 00:43:54,530
He wanted...

488
00:43:54,710 --> 00:43:56,370
...me.

489
00:43:56,940 --> 00:44:01,280
I don't know why. But he wasgonna use this man to get to me.

490
00:44:02,550 --> 00:44:04,710
But, I mean, it was only a dream, right?

491
00:44:05,090 --> 00:44:06,710
Yes.

492
00:44:06,890 --> 00:44:08,450
It's just a dream.

493
00:44:09,190 --> 00:44:10,620
Look, Harry.

494
00:44:10,790 --> 00:44:14,250
The Death Eaters at the World Cup,your name rising from that goblet...

495
00:44:14,430 --> 00:44:18,420
...these are not just coincidences.Hogwarts isn't safe anymore.

496
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:19,690
What are you saying?

497
00:44:19,870 --> 00:44:24,130
I'm saying the devils are insidethe walls. Igor Karkaroff?

498
00:44:24,310 --> 00:44:28,710
He was a Death Eater. And no one,no one stops being a Death Eater.

499
00:44:29,140 --> 00:44:34,270
Then there's Barty Crouch. Heart of stone.Sent his own son to Azkaban.

500
00:44:39,090 --> 00:44:41,180
You think one of themput my name in the goblet?

501
00:44:41,360 --> 00:44:43,650
I haven't a clue who put your namein that goblet...

502
00:44:43,820 --> 00:44:47,780
...but whoever did is no friend to you.People die in this tournament.

503
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:51,450
-I'm not ready for this, Sirius.-You don't have a choice.

504
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:57,400
-Someone's coming.-Keep your friends close, Harry.

505
00:45:00,710 --> 00:45:02,040
Who were you talking to?

506
00:45:02,210 --> 00:45:05,270
-What? Who says I was talking to anyone?-I heard voices.

507
00:45:05,550 --> 00:45:09,540
Maybe you're imagining things.Wouldn't be the first time.

508
00:45:10,080 --> 00:45:13,420
You're probably just practicingfor your next interview, I expect.

509
00:45:39,350 --> 00:45:40,970
Amazing.

510
00:45:42,950 --> 00:45:46,650
-Amazing!-Neville. You're doing it again.

511
00:45:47,220 --> 00:45:48,620
Right, sorry.

512
00:45:49,490 --> 00:45:52,480
"Magical Water Plantsof the Highland Lochs"?

513
00:45:52,660 --> 00:45:55,820
Moody gave it to me.That day we had tea.

514
00:45:57,330 --> 00:45:59,060
It's already been through enough people.

515
00:45:59,230 --> 00:46:01,330
Why don't you just goand talk to him yourself?

516
00:46:02,800 --> 00:46:05,140
Ron, this is your problem, not mine.

517
00:46:05,310 --> 00:46:07,400
What do you want me to say again?

518
00:46:07,580 --> 00:46:08,910
Go.

519
00:46:11,850 --> 00:46:16,010
Ronald would like me to tell youthat Seamus told him...

520
00:46:16,580 --> 00:46:20,180
...that Dean was told by Parvatithat Hagrid's looking for you.

521
00:46:20,350 --> 00:46:22,790
Is that right? Well, you--

522
00:46:22,960 --> 00:46:24,020
What?

523
00:46:29,130 --> 00:46:32,070
-Are you sure you won't do this?-Do it.

524
00:46:34,870 --> 00:46:37,840
Dean was told by Parvati that....

525
00:46:39,070 --> 00:46:41,300
Please don't ask me to say it again.

526
00:46:41,680 --> 00:46:43,140
Hagrid's looking for you.

527
00:46:43,640 --> 00:46:46,700
-Well, you can tell Ronald---I'm not an owl!

528
00:46:57,260 --> 00:46:59,520
Did you bring your father's cloak,like I asked you?

529
00:46:59,690 --> 00:47:02,290
Yeah, I brought the cloak.Hagrid, where are we going?

530
00:47:02,460 --> 00:47:03,860
You'll see soon enough.

531
00:47:04,030 --> 00:47:06,230
Now pay attention, this is important.

532
00:47:07,970 --> 00:47:09,440
What's with the flower?

533
00:47:10,470 --> 00:47:12,870
Hagrid, have you combed your hair?

534
00:47:13,270 --> 00:47:15,000
As a matter of fact, I have.

535
00:47:15,440 --> 00:47:18,380
You might like to try the same thingnow and again.

536
00:47:26,890 --> 00:47:28,350
Hagrid?

537
00:47:32,260 --> 00:47:34,160
The cloak! Put the cloak on!

538
00:47:40,700 --> 00:47:44,100
-Bonsoir, Olympe.-Oh, Hagrid.

539
00:47:44,270 --> 00:47:48,000
I thought perhaps you weren't coming.I thought perhaps...

540
00:47:48,180 --> 00:47:50,840
...you had forgotten me.

541
00:47:51,010 --> 00:47:52,980
Couldn't forget you, Olympe.

542
00:47:53,610 --> 00:47:55,450
What is it you wanted to show me?

543
00:47:57,120 --> 00:48:00,350
When we spoke earlier,you sounded so...

544
00:48:00,690 --> 00:48:02,180
...exhilarated.

545
00:48:02,760 --> 00:48:05,590
You'll be glad you came. Trust me.

546
00:48:16,170 --> 00:48:17,930
Can we get closer?

547
00:48:25,750 --> 00:48:27,210
Dragons?

548
00:48:27,380 --> 00:48:28,870
That's the first task?

549
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:31,310
-You're joking.-Come on, Harry.

550
00:48:32,590 --> 00:48:35,610
These are seriouslymisunderstood creatures.

551
00:48:36,720 --> 00:48:38,190
Oh, crikey!

552
00:48:38,690 --> 00:48:43,690
Although, I have to admit,that Horntail is a right nasty piece of work.

553
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:46,830
Poor Ron nearly faintedjust seeing him, you know.

554
00:48:48,340 --> 00:48:50,360
-Ron was here?-Oh, sure.

555
00:48:50,540 --> 00:48:54,070
His brother Charlie helpedto bring him over from Romania.

556
00:48:54,240 --> 00:48:55,670
Didn't Ron tell you that?

557
00:48:57,610 --> 00:48:59,010
No, he didn't.

558
00:48:59,750 --> 00:49:01,610
He didn't tell me a thing.

559
00:49:11,560 --> 00:49:14,650
-You cheat, Potter.-You stink, Potter.

560
00:49:16,160 --> 00:49:18,830
-Good luck, Potter.-Potter stinks!

561
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:21,660
-Cedric rules.-Thanks.

562
00:49:22,740 --> 00:49:24,400
Like the badge?

563
00:49:24,970 --> 00:49:26,700
Excuse me.

564
00:49:30,880 --> 00:49:32,350
Harry.

565
00:49:32,910 --> 00:49:34,880
Hey! Read the badge, Potter!

566
00:49:35,050 --> 00:49:36,540
Can I have a word?

567
00:49:37,520 --> 00:49:39,380
-All right.-You stink, Potter!

568
00:49:39,550 --> 00:49:42,550
-Potter, you stink!-Harry Potter smells!

569
00:49:45,060 --> 00:49:47,620
Dragons. That's the first task.

570
00:49:47,800 --> 00:49:50,920
-They've got one for each of us.-Come on, Ced!

571
00:49:51,100 --> 00:49:53,120
Are you serious?

572
00:49:53,900 --> 00:49:56,930
And Fleur and Krum, do they--?

573
00:49:57,100 --> 00:49:59,370
-Yes.-Come on, Ced, leave him.

574
00:49:59,540 --> 00:50:01,010
-Right.-He's not worth it.

575
00:50:01,180 --> 00:50:03,670
-Read the badges, Potter!-Hey, listen. About the badges.

576
00:50:03,840 --> 00:50:06,870
-I've asked them not to wear them, but---Don't worry about it.

577
00:50:07,050 --> 00:50:09,480
It's not like I tryto blow things up, exactly.

578
00:50:10,180 --> 00:50:11,650
It just happens a fair bit.

579
00:50:11,820 --> 00:50:14,880
You have to admit, though,fire's pretty fascinating.

580
00:50:15,060 --> 00:50:16,890
You're a right foul git, you know that?

581
00:50:17,060 --> 00:50:19,320
-You think so?-I know so.

582
00:50:19,490 --> 00:50:20,820
Anything else?

583
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:24,490
-Yeah. Stay away from me.-Fine.

584
00:50:26,870 --> 00:50:30,460
-There's Potter. Cheat.-Why so tense, Potter?

585
00:50:31,240 --> 00:50:33,640
My father and I have a bet, you see.

586
00:50:33,810 --> 00:50:37,000
I don't think you're gonna last1 0 minutes in this tournament.

587
00:50:39,580 --> 00:50:42,520
He disagrees.He thinks you won't last five.

588
00:50:42,680 --> 00:50:45,810
I don't give a damnwhat your father thinks, Malfoy.

589
00:50:46,790 --> 00:50:50,780
He's vile and cruel.And you're just pathetic.

590
00:50:51,690 --> 00:50:54,290
-Pathetic?-Oh, no, you don't, sonny!

591
00:50:56,460 --> 00:50:59,360
I'll teach you to curse someonewhen their back is turned!

592
00:50:59,530 --> 00:51:03,370
You stinking, cowardly, scummy...

593
00:51:03,540 --> 00:51:05,270
-Professor Moody!-...back-shooting--

594
00:51:05,440 --> 00:51:08,340
-What are you doing?-Teaching.

595
00:51:09,380 --> 00:51:13,510
-ls that a--? Is that a student?-Technically, it's a ferret.

596
00:51:19,150 --> 00:51:21,090
Stand still! Stand still!

597
00:51:32,070 --> 00:51:34,260
-My father will hear about this!-ls that a threat?

598
00:51:34,440 --> 00:51:36,370
-Professor Moody!-ls that a threat?

599
00:51:36,540 --> 00:51:38,400
Professor!

600
00:51:38,570 --> 00:51:42,130
I could tell you stories about your fatherthat would curl even your greasy hair!

601
00:51:42,310 --> 00:51:45,010
-Alastor! Alastor.-lt doesn't end here!

602
00:51:45,180 --> 00:51:48,980
We never use transfigurationas a punishment!

603
00:51:49,150 --> 00:51:51,340
Surely Dumbledore told you that.

604
00:51:51,890 --> 00:51:56,350
-He might've mentioned it.-Well, you will do well to remember it.

605
00:51:57,460 --> 00:51:58,930
Away!

606
00:52:02,030 --> 00:52:04,220
You. Come with me.

607
00:52:39,470 --> 00:52:41,530
That's a Foe-Glass.

608
00:52:42,270 --> 00:52:44,430
Lets me keep an eye on my enemies.

609
00:52:44,840 --> 00:52:49,240
If I can see the whites of their eyes,they're standing right behind me.

610
00:52:53,410 --> 00:52:55,880
Wouldn't even bother telling youwhat's in there.

611
00:52:56,050 --> 00:52:58,080
You wouldn't believe it if I did.

612
00:52:58,350 --> 00:53:00,050
Now...

613
00:53:01,720 --> 00:53:04,560
...what are you going to doabout your dragon?

614
00:53:08,460 --> 00:53:10,760
Well, you know, I just thought l'd....

615
00:53:12,230 --> 00:53:13,720
Sit.

616
00:53:17,440 --> 00:53:18,840
Listen to me, Potter.

617
00:53:19,840 --> 00:53:21,000
Your pal Diggory?

618
00:53:21,180 --> 00:53:25,640
By your age, he could turn a whistleinto a watch and have it sing you the time.

619
00:53:26,780 --> 00:53:28,040
Miss Delacour?

620
00:53:28,450 --> 00:53:31,180
She's as much a fairy princess as I am.

621
00:53:31,690 --> 00:53:35,250
As for Krum, his headmay be filled with sawdust...

622
00:53:35,420 --> 00:53:37,580
...but Karkaroff's is not.

623
00:53:37,760 --> 00:53:39,590
They'll have a strategy.

624
00:53:39,760 --> 00:53:43,290
And you can bet that it willplay to Krum's strengths.

625
00:53:48,070 --> 00:53:49,630
Come on, Potter.

626
00:53:49,800 --> 00:53:51,900
What are your strengths?

627
00:53:53,470 --> 00:53:54,840
I don't know.

628
00:53:55,010 --> 00:53:57,810
Well, I can fly.I mean, I'm a fair flyer. But l....

629
00:53:57,980 --> 00:54:02,010
-Better than fair, the way I heard it.-But I'm not allowed a broom.

630
00:54:02,180 --> 00:54:05,810
You're allowed a wand.

631
00:54:12,260 --> 00:54:13,730
Bets! Place your bets!

632
00:54:13,890 --> 00:54:16,060
Bets taken! Bets taken here!

633
00:54:16,230 --> 00:54:19,170
Step up, folks! Who fancies a flutterin today's bloodbath?

634
00:54:19,330 --> 00:54:22,200
Smart money's on Krum to survive!Any bets?

635
00:54:22,370 --> 00:54:23,860
Yes, sir?

636
00:54:24,200 --> 00:54:26,930
Ten-to-1 for Fleur. There you go.Thank you very much.

637
00:54:27,440 --> 00:54:29,380
Your attention, please.

638
00:54:29,610 --> 00:54:32,200
This is a great day for all of us.

639
00:54:35,650 --> 00:54:39,880
Each of the three tasks involvesvery considerable danger.

640
00:54:40,050 --> 00:54:42,750
Please keep your seats at all times.

641
00:54:42,920 --> 00:54:45,650
This will minimize any risksyou may be exposed to.

642
00:54:45,830 --> 00:54:49,260
-Harry? Is that you?-Yeah.

643
00:54:49,430 --> 00:54:51,120
I'm sure we all wish our champions...

644
00:54:51,300 --> 00:54:54,360
-How are you feeling? Okay?-... the greatest of luck.

645
00:54:56,670 --> 00:55:00,070
The key is to concentrate.After that, you just have to--

646
00:55:00,240 --> 00:55:02,070
Battle a dragon.

647
00:55:06,380 --> 00:55:08,870
Young love.

648
00:55:09,580 --> 00:55:10,850
How...

649
00:55:13,320 --> 00:55:14,620
...stirring.

650
00:55:17,290 --> 00:55:20,450
If everything goes unfortunately today...

651
00:55:20,630 --> 00:55:23,390
...you two may evenmake the front page.

652
00:55:23,560 --> 00:55:25,790
You have no business here.

653
00:55:25,970 --> 00:55:27,990
This tent is for champions...

654
00:55:28,340 --> 00:55:30,030
...and friends.

655
00:55:32,840 --> 00:55:37,000
No matter. We've got what we wanted.

656
00:55:40,150 --> 00:55:42,950
Good day, champions.Gather round, please.

657
00:55:43,120 --> 00:55:47,310
Now, you've waited, you've wondered,and at last the moment has arrived.

658
00:55:47,490 --> 00:55:50,720
A moment only four of youcan fully appreciate.

659
00:55:50,890 --> 00:55:53,020
What are you doing here, Miss Granger?

660
00:55:54,330 --> 00:55:55,990
Sorry, I'll just go.

661
00:55:56,160 --> 00:55:57,760
Barty, the bag.

662
00:55:58,130 --> 00:56:00,360
Champions, in a circle around me.

663
00:56:00,530 --> 00:56:03,630
Miss Delacour, over here. Mr. Krum.

664
00:56:03,800 --> 00:56:07,740
And, Potter, Mr. Potter, over here.That's right. Now...

665
00:56:07,910 --> 00:56:10,340
...Miss Delacour, if you will.

666
00:56:14,410 --> 00:56:16,080
The Welsh Green.

667
00:56:20,720 --> 00:56:22,050
Mr. Krum.

668
00:56:25,030 --> 00:56:26,930
The Chinese Fireball.

669
00:56:33,400 --> 00:56:35,800
The Swedish Short-Snout.

670
00:56:36,270 --> 00:56:38,260
-Which leaves....-The Horntail.

671
00:56:38,440 --> 00:56:40,700
-What's that, boy?-Nothing.

672
00:56:44,110 --> 00:56:46,510
The Hungarian Horntail.

673
00:56:48,680 --> 00:56:51,810
These represent fourvery real dragons...

674
00:56:51,990 --> 00:56:55,050
...each of which has been givena golden egg to protect.

675
00:56:55,220 --> 00:56:57,690
Your objective is simple:

676
00:56:57,860 --> 00:56:59,350
Collect the egg.

677
00:56:59,530 --> 00:57:02,520
This you must do,for each egg contains a clue...

678
00:57:02,700 --> 00:57:06,190
...without which you cannot hopeto proceed to the next task.

679
00:57:06,370 --> 00:57:07,700
Any questions?

680
00:57:08,740 --> 00:57:11,400
Very well. Good luck, champions.

681
00:57:11,570 --> 00:57:14,400
Mr. Diggory, at the sound of the cannon,you may--

682
00:57:23,020 --> 00:57:26,850
Diggory! Diggory! Diggory!

683
00:57:38,430 --> 00:57:41,800
Three of our championshave now faced their dragons...

684
00:57:41,970 --> 00:57:45,460
...and so each one of themwill proceed to the next task.

685
00:57:46,040 --> 00:57:49,130
And now our fourth and final contestant.

686
00:57:51,110 --> 00:57:54,670
Harry! Harry! Harry!

687
00:59:01,780 --> 00:59:04,720
Your wand, Harry! Your wand!

688
00:59:05,220 --> 00:59:07,240
Accio Firebolt!

689
00:59:36,250 --> 00:59:38,410
-Yeah!-Yes!

690
00:59:47,330 --> 00:59:48,760
Oh, my God.

691
00:59:58,410 --> 01:00:01,700
-Yeah!-Yeah! Well done, dragon!

692
01:02:33,690 --> 01:02:35,850
Yes! Yes!

693
01:02:59,090 --> 01:03:01,780
-Yes, Harry!-Knew you wouldn't die, Harry. Lose a leg.

694
01:03:01,960 --> 01:03:03,890
-Or an arm.-Pack it in altogether?

695
01:03:04,060 --> 01:03:05,820
-Never!-Never!

696
01:03:07,930 --> 01:03:09,260
Shush!

697
01:03:09,730 --> 01:03:12,390
Go on, Harry. What's the clue?

698
01:03:13,430 --> 01:03:16,270
-Who wants me to open it?-Yes!

699
01:03:17,070 --> 01:03:19,600
-Do you want me to open it?-Yes!

700
01:03:30,780 --> 01:03:33,180
What the bloody hell was that?

701
01:03:37,320 --> 01:03:40,050
All right, everyone!Go back to your knitting.

702
01:03:40,230 --> 01:03:44,250
This is gonna be uncomfortable enoughwithout all you nosy sods listening in.

703
01:03:47,430 --> 01:03:51,430
I reckon you have to be barking madto put your own name in the Goblet of Fire.

704
01:03:51,770 --> 01:03:54,500
Caught on, have you?Took you long enough.

705
01:03:55,640 --> 01:03:57,740
I wasn't the only onewho thought you'd done it.

706
01:03:57,910 --> 01:04:00,180
Everyone was saying it behind your back.

707
01:04:02,380 --> 01:04:05,610
Brilliant. That makes mefeel loads better.

708
01:04:06,550 --> 01:04:09,950
-Least I warned you about the dragons.-Hagrid warned me about the dragons.

709
01:04:10,120 --> 01:04:11,590
No, no, no, I did.

710
01:04:11,760 --> 01:04:14,780
No, don't you remember?I told Hermione to tell you...

711
01:04:14,960 --> 01:04:19,020
...that Seamus told me that Parvatitold Dean that Hagrid was looking for you.

712
01:04:19,200 --> 01:04:23,140
Seamus never actually told me anything,so it was really me all along.

713
01:04:24,140 --> 01:04:27,130
I thought we'd be all right, you know...

714
01:04:27,370 --> 01:04:29,360
...after you'd figured that out.

715
01:04:29,740 --> 01:04:32,410
Who--? Who could possiblyfigure that out?

716
01:04:33,080 --> 01:04:34,510
That's completely mental.

717
01:04:34,680 --> 01:04:37,710
Yeah. Isn't it?

718
01:04:37,880 --> 01:04:39,910
I suppose I was a bit distraught.

719
01:04:42,520 --> 01:04:44,220
Boys.

720
01:05:08,680 --> 01:05:10,110
-Hi, Harry.-Hi, Harry.

721
01:05:13,750 --> 01:05:16,350
Cho, Harry's looking at you.

722
01:05:20,290 --> 01:05:21,990
Shush.

723
01:05:22,700 --> 01:05:24,060
Look at this!

724
01:05:26,070 --> 01:05:28,560
I can't believe it! She's done it again.

725
01:05:29,600 --> 01:05:31,830
"Miss Granger,a plain but ambitious girl...

726
01:05:32,010 --> 01:05:34,770
...seems to be developing a tastefor famous wizards.

727
01:05:34,940 --> 01:05:37,210
Her latest prey, sources report...

728
01:05:37,380 --> 01:05:41,010
...is none other than theBulgarian bonbon, Viktor Krum.

729
01:05:41,310 --> 01:05:45,250
No word yet on how Harry Potter'staking this latest emotional blow."

730
01:05:46,620 --> 01:05:48,550
Parcel for you, Mr. Weasley.

731
01:05:48,720 --> 01:05:50,210
Thank you, Nigel.

732
01:05:55,030 --> 01:05:57,860
Not now, Nigel. Later.

733
01:05:59,700 --> 01:06:01,220
Go on.

734
01:06:06,570 --> 01:06:09,340
I told him I'd get him Harry's autograph.

735
01:06:11,540 --> 01:06:13,310
Oh, look, Mum's sent me something.

736
01:06:21,450 --> 01:06:23,290
Mum sent me a dress.

737
01:06:23,460 --> 01:06:27,260
Well, it does match your eyes.Is there a bonnet?

738
01:06:27,730 --> 01:06:29,560
Nose down, Harry.

739
01:06:30,100 --> 01:06:34,060
-Ginny, these must be for you.-I'm not wearing that, it's ghastly.

740
01:06:35,800 --> 01:06:37,630
What are you on about?

741
01:06:37,800 --> 01:06:39,740
They're not for Ginny.

742
01:06:39,910 --> 01:06:41,310
They're for you.

743
01:06:42,280 --> 01:06:46,040
-Dress robes.-Dress robes? For what?

744
01:06:47,280 --> 01:06:49,440
The Yule Ball...

745
01:06:49,620 --> 01:06:54,950
...has been a traditionof the Triwizard Tournament...

746
01:06:55,690 --> 01:06:57,750
...since its inception.

747
01:06:58,420 --> 01:07:02,290
On Christmas Eve night,we and our guests...

748
01:07:02,460 --> 01:07:04,120
...gather in the Great Hall...

749
01:07:04,300 --> 01:07:08,360
...for a night of well-mannered frivolity.

750
01:07:09,900 --> 01:07:12,170
As representatives of the host school...

751
01:07:12,340 --> 01:07:17,440
...I expect each and every one of youto put your best foot forward.

752
01:07:17,740 --> 01:07:20,370
And I mean this literally, because...

753
01:07:20,550 --> 01:07:24,980
...the Yule Ball is, first and foremost...

754
01:07:25,850 --> 01:07:27,340
...a dance.

755
01:07:31,590 --> 01:07:33,390
Silence!

756
01:07:33,590 --> 01:07:36,590
The house of Godric Gryffindorhas commanded the respect...

757
01:07:36,760 --> 01:07:39,390
...of the wizard worldfor nearly 1 0 centuries.

758
01:07:39,570 --> 01:07:43,630
I will not have you, in the course ofa single evening, besmirching that name...

759
01:07:43,800 --> 01:07:48,000
...by behaving like a babbling,bumbling band of baboons.

760
01:07:48,740 --> 01:07:50,710
Try saying that five times fast, huh?

761
01:07:50,880 --> 01:07:52,370
Now, to dance...

762
01:07:52,550 --> 01:07:56,240
...is to let the body breathe.

763
01:07:56,420 --> 01:07:59,750
Inside every girl,a secret swan slumbers...

764
01:07:59,920 --> 01:08:02,290
...Ionging to burst forth and take flight.

765
01:08:02,460 --> 01:08:06,450
Something's about to burst out of EloiseMidgen, but I don't think it's a swan.

766
01:08:06,630 --> 01:08:09,750
Inside every boy,a lordly lion prepared to prance.

767
01:08:09,930 --> 01:08:12,160
-Mr. Weasley.-Yes?

768
01:08:12,330 --> 01:08:14,770
Will you join me, please?

769
01:08:19,370 --> 01:08:22,900
Now, place your right hand on my waist.

770
01:08:23,080 --> 01:08:25,640
-Where?-My waist.

771
01:08:25,810 --> 01:08:28,370
And extend your arm.

772
01:08:28,820 --> 01:08:30,780
Mr. Filch, if you please.

773
01:08:33,850 --> 01:08:35,840
One, two, three.

774
01:08:36,020 --> 01:08:39,510
One, two, three. One, two, three.

775
01:08:43,230 --> 01:08:45,360
Never gonna let him forget this, are you?

776
01:08:45,530 --> 01:08:46,690
-Never.-Never.

777
01:08:46,870 --> 01:08:50,730
Everybody come together.Boys, on your feet!

778
01:09:13,830 --> 01:09:15,760
Why do they have to travel in packs?

779
01:09:15,930 --> 01:09:18,590
How are you supposed to get oneon their own to ask them?

780
01:09:26,440 --> 01:09:29,930
Blimey, Harry. You've slayed dragons.If you can't get a date, who can?

781
01:09:30,110 --> 01:09:32,370
I think I'd take the dragon right now.

782
01:09:38,580 --> 01:09:40,140
I take after my mum.

783
01:09:40,320 --> 01:09:44,260
Though I didn't know her very well.She left when I was about 3.

784
01:09:44,420 --> 01:09:46,360
No, not the maternal sort, her.

785
01:09:46,530 --> 01:09:50,090
Broke me dad's heart, though.He was a tiny little fella, my dad.

786
01:09:50,260 --> 01:09:54,790
I could pick him up at the age of 6 withone hand and put him up on the dresser.

787
01:09:54,970 --> 01:09:57,300
He laughed so hard at that.

788
01:09:59,370 --> 01:10:01,240
Very funny.

789
01:10:07,180 --> 01:10:10,910
And then he diedjust when I started school, so....

790
01:10:11,080 --> 01:10:14,110
So I sort of had to makeme own way, as it were.

791
01:10:14,550 --> 01:10:16,780
But enough of me. What about you?

792
01:10:33,970 --> 01:10:39,070
This is mad. At this rate, we'll bethe only ones in our year without dates.

793
01:10:41,350 --> 01:10:44,080
Well, us and Neville.

794
01:10:44,250 --> 01:10:46,910
Yeah, but, then again,he can take himself.

795
01:10:47,650 --> 01:10:50,990
It might interest you to knowthat Neville's already got someone.

796
01:10:53,460 --> 01:10:55,220
Now I'm really depressed.

797
01:11:01,070 --> 01:11:04,530
"Get a move on or all the good oneswill have gone."

798
01:11:06,570 --> 01:11:08,540
Who you going with, then?

799
01:11:11,280 --> 01:11:12,970
-Oi, Angelina?-What?

800
01:11:13,150 --> 01:11:18,450
Do you wanna go to the ball with me?

801
01:11:18,780 --> 01:11:20,510
To the ball?

802
01:11:20,690 --> 01:11:22,150
Yeah, all right.

803
01:11:25,860 --> 01:11:27,420
Oi, Hermione.

804
01:11:27,590 --> 01:11:29,220
You're a girl.

805
01:11:29,400 --> 01:11:30,730
Very well spotted.

806
01:11:30,900 --> 01:11:32,830
Come with one of us?

807
01:11:37,470 --> 01:11:40,370
Come on. It's one thing for a bloketo show up alone.

808
01:11:40,540 --> 01:11:42,030
For a girl, it's just sad.

809
01:11:42,210 --> 01:11:45,970
I won't be going alone, because,believe it or not, someone's asked me!

810
01:11:52,920 --> 01:11:54,910
And I said yes!

811
01:11:56,760 --> 01:11:58,350
Bloody hell.

812
01:11:58,520 --> 01:12:00,190
She's lying, right?

813
01:12:00,360 --> 01:12:01,590
If you say so.

814
01:12:02,300 --> 01:12:05,590
Look, we've just gottagrit our teeth and do it.

815
01:12:05,770 --> 01:12:09,670
Tonight, when we get back to the commonroom, we'll both have partners. Agreed?

816
01:12:09,840 --> 01:12:11,390
Agreed.

817
01:12:35,760 --> 01:12:37,090
-Cho!-Harry!

818
01:12:40,670 --> 01:12:43,400
Watch yourself on the stairs.It's a bit icy at the top.

819
01:12:43,570 --> 01:12:45,160
Okay, thanks.

820
01:12:49,610 --> 01:12:50,670
Cho?

821
01:12:51,610 --> 01:12:53,170
Yes?

822
01:12:54,550 --> 01:12:56,780
Well, I just wondered if you--

823
01:12:56,950 --> 01:12:59,610
I wondered if maybeyou wanted to go to the ball with me.

824
01:13:01,420 --> 01:13:03,680
Sorry, I didn't catch that.

825
01:13:04,590 --> 01:13:09,490
I was just wondering if maybeyou wanted to go to the ball with me.

826
01:13:15,530 --> 01:13:17,090
Harry...

827
01:13:17,270 --> 01:13:20,100
...I'm sorry, but someone'salready asked me.

828
01:13:21,110 --> 01:13:22,540
And....

829
01:13:23,210 --> 01:13:26,440
Well, I've said I'll go with him.

830
01:13:28,110 --> 01:13:30,670
Okay. Yeah. Great.

831
01:13:31,980 --> 01:13:34,710
Fine. No problem.

832
01:13:35,020 --> 01:13:36,610
Okay. Good.

833
01:13:37,890 --> 01:13:39,620
Harry?

834
01:13:40,260 --> 01:13:42,060
I really am...

835
01:13:42,230 --> 01:13:43,860
...sorry.

836
01:13:53,640 --> 01:13:55,130
It's all right, Ron.

837
01:13:55,310 --> 01:13:58,510
It's okay, Ron. It's all right.It doesn't matter.

838
01:13:58,680 --> 01:14:00,540
What happened to you?

839
01:14:00,810 --> 01:14:02,970
He just asked Fleur Delacour out.

840
01:14:03,150 --> 01:14:05,640
-What?-What did she say?

841
01:14:05,820 --> 01:14:07,180
No, of course.

842
01:14:08,750 --> 01:14:12,090
-She said yes?-Don't be silly.

843
01:14:12,490 --> 01:14:16,930
There she was, walking by.You know how I like it when they walk.

844
01:14:17,660 --> 01:14:21,290
I couldn't help it.It just sort of slipped out.

845
01:14:21,470 --> 01:14:24,930
Actually, he sort of screamed at her.It was a bit frightening.

846
01:14:26,110 --> 01:14:29,700
-And what did you do then?-What else? I ran for it.

847
01:14:29,880 --> 01:14:33,610
I'm not cut out for this, Harry.I don't know what got into me.

848
01:14:33,780 --> 01:14:35,010
-Hi, Harry.-Hi, Harry.

849
01:14:35,180 --> 01:14:38,240
I always liked looking at themfrom behind.

850
01:14:39,590 --> 01:14:42,150
She's never gonna forgive me, ever.

851
01:14:42,790 --> 01:14:43,780
Hey!

852
01:15:00,870 --> 01:15:02,570
Bloody hell.

853
01:15:04,810 --> 01:15:06,570
Bloody hell.

854
01:15:10,080 --> 01:15:11,380
Bloody....

855
01:15:11,550 --> 01:15:12,780
Oh, bloody....

856
01:15:16,490 --> 01:15:19,190
What are those? What are those?

857
01:15:19,360 --> 01:15:22,380
-My dress robes.-Well, they're all right!

858
01:15:22,560 --> 01:15:25,500
No lace. No dodgy little collar.

859
01:15:25,660 --> 01:15:27,600
Well, I expect yours are more traditional.

860
01:15:27,770 --> 01:15:32,800
Traditional?! They're ancient!I look like my Great Aunt Tessie!

861
01:15:35,170 --> 01:15:38,230
I smell like my Great Aunt Tessie.

862
01:15:42,980 --> 01:15:44,810
Murder me, Harry.

863
01:15:46,220 --> 01:15:47,780
Leave it alone!

864
01:15:48,750 --> 01:15:52,190
Poor kid. I bet she's alone in her room,crying her eyes out.

865
01:15:52,360 --> 01:15:54,830
-Who?-Hermione, of course.

866
01:15:54,990 --> 01:15:58,590
Come on, Harry, why do you think shewouldn't tell us who she's coming with?

867
01:15:58,760 --> 01:16:00,960
Because we'd take the mickey out of herif she did.

868
01:16:01,130 --> 01:16:06,230
Nobody asked her. Would've taken hermyself if she wasn't so bloody proud.

869
01:16:07,210 --> 01:16:08,610
-Hello, boys.-Hello, boys.

870
01:16:08,770 --> 01:16:10,610
Don't you look...

871
01:16:11,180 --> 01:16:12,370
...dashing.

872
01:16:12,950 --> 01:16:16,110
There you are, Potter.Are you and Miss Patil ready?

873
01:16:16,280 --> 01:16:18,110
-Ready, professor?-To dance.

874
01:16:18,280 --> 01:16:21,310
It's traditional that the three champions--Well, in this case, four.

875
01:16:21,490 --> 01:16:22,550
--are the first to dance.

876
01:16:22,890 --> 01:16:25,520
-Surely I told you that.-No.

877
01:16:26,090 --> 01:16:27,820
Well, now you know.

878
01:16:29,330 --> 01:16:33,630
As for you, Mr. Weasley, you may proceedinto the Great Hall with Miss Patil.

879
01:16:33,800 --> 01:16:36,200
-Oh, there you are.-Come on, then.

880
01:16:36,370 --> 01:16:37,860
Come along this way.

881
01:16:42,740 --> 01:16:44,570
Oh, come on.

882
01:16:45,410 --> 01:16:47,400
-Hi.-Now, I need you all to line up...

883
01:16:47,580 --> 01:16:50,950
...in the procession, please.Oh, you are very late.

884
01:16:53,150 --> 01:16:55,550
This way. This way. Come along.

885
01:16:57,260 --> 01:16:59,490
She looks beautiful!

886
01:16:59,660 --> 01:17:01,250
Yeah, she does.

887
01:17:48,640 --> 01:17:52,200
Is that Hermione Granger?With Viktor Krum?

888
01:17:52,850 --> 01:17:55,410
No. Absolutely not.

889
01:18:00,120 --> 01:18:01,680
Hi!

890
01:18:10,430 --> 01:18:12,420
Harry, take my waist.

891
01:18:13,300 --> 01:18:14,730
-What?-Now!

892
01:19:21,300 --> 01:19:23,170
Are you ready?

893
01:19:23,740 --> 01:19:26,000
Move your body like a hairy troll

894
01:19:26,770 --> 01:19:29,240
Learning to rock and roll

895
01:19:29,640 --> 01:19:32,240
Spin around like a crazy elf

896
01:19:32,750 --> 01:19:34,980
Dancing by himself

897
01:19:35,280 --> 01:19:38,620
Boogie down like a unicorn

898
01:19:38,790 --> 01:19:41,220
No stopping till the break of dawn

899
01:19:41,390 --> 01:19:44,220
Put your hands up in the air

900
01:19:44,430 --> 01:19:47,190
Like an ogre who just don 't care

901
01:19:47,900 --> 01:19:50,560
Can you dance like a Hippogriff?

902
01:19:52,900 --> 01:19:55,100
Ruddy pumpkinhead, isn't he?

903
01:19:57,270 --> 01:20:00,670
I don't think it was the booksthat had him going to the library.

904
01:20:02,610 --> 01:20:04,130
May I have your arm?

905
01:20:04,310 --> 01:20:07,040
Arm. Leg. I'm yours.

906
01:20:32,940 --> 01:20:34,530
Hot, isn't it?

907
01:20:35,210 --> 01:20:38,540
Viktor's gone to go and get drinks.Would you care to join us?

908
01:20:38,710 --> 01:20:42,410
No, we'd not care to join you and Viktor.

909
01:20:44,090 --> 01:20:46,420
What's got your wand in a knot?

910
01:20:46,720 --> 01:20:50,420
He's a Durmstrang.You're fraternizing with the enemy.

911
01:20:50,590 --> 01:20:54,150
The enemy?Who was it wanting his autograph?

912
01:20:54,860 --> 01:20:57,300
Besides, the whole pointof the tournament...

913
01:20:57,470 --> 01:21:00,990
...is internationalmagical cooperation...

914
01:21:01,570 --> 01:21:03,130
...to make friends.

915
01:21:03,800 --> 01:21:06,970
I think he's got a bit morethan friendship on his mind.

916
01:21:16,950 --> 01:21:19,280
Are you going to ask meto dance or not?

917
01:21:19,450 --> 01:21:20,890
No.

918
01:21:29,130 --> 01:21:31,560
-He's using you.-How dare you?!

919
01:21:31,730 --> 01:21:35,930
-Besides, I can take care of myself.-I doubt it. He's way too old.

920
01:21:36,100 --> 01:21:39,770
-What?! What? That's what you think?-Yeah, that's what I think.

921
01:21:39,940 --> 01:21:42,070
You know the solution then, don't you?

922
01:21:42,240 --> 01:21:44,230
-Go on.-Next time there's a ball...

923
01:21:44,410 --> 01:21:47,540
...pluck up the courage and ask mebefore somebody else does!

924
01:21:47,720 --> 01:21:49,740
And not as a last resort.

925
01:21:49,920 --> 01:21:54,120
Well, that's-- I mean,that's just completely off the point.

926
01:21:54,290 --> 01:21:55,620
Harry.

927
01:21:56,090 --> 01:21:57,390
Where have you been?

928
01:21:57,560 --> 01:22:00,050
Never mind! Off to bed, both of you.

929
01:22:02,860 --> 01:22:06,890
-They get scary when they get older.-Ron, you spoiled everything!

930
01:22:07,070 --> 01:22:08,930
What's this about?

931
01:22:13,210 --> 01:22:16,200
No, don 't let

932
01:22:18,010 --> 01:22:22,350
This magic die

933
01:22:24,120 --> 01:22:26,880
The answer's there

934
01:23:25,210 --> 01:23:27,310
Let me see it again.

935
01:23:28,620 --> 01:23:31,550
Yes, the time is close now.

936
01:23:36,220 --> 01:23:38,090
Harry, at last!

937
01:23:39,390 --> 01:23:44,730
Step aside, Wormtail,so I can give our guest a proper greeting.

938
01:23:55,340 --> 01:23:56,740
You all right, Harry?

939
01:23:58,180 --> 01:23:59,940
I just got in.

940
01:24:00,550 --> 01:24:01,780
Me.

941
01:24:13,060 --> 01:24:16,330
Harry, you told meyou'd figured the egg out weeks ago.

942
01:24:16,500 --> 01:24:20,700
-The task is two days from now.-Really? I had no idea.

943
01:24:22,240 --> 01:24:24,030
I suppose Viktor'salready figured it out.

944
01:24:24,210 --> 01:24:27,040
Wouldn't know. We don't actuallytalk about the tournament.

945
01:24:28,240 --> 01:24:32,840
Actually, we don't really talk at all.Viktor's more of a physical being.

946
01:24:36,580 --> 01:24:39,780
I just mean he's notparticularly loquacious.

947
01:24:40,250 --> 01:24:42,480
Mostly, he watches me study.

948
01:24:43,290 --> 01:24:45,380
It's a bit annoying, actually.

949
01:24:46,760 --> 01:24:49,460
You are trying to figure this egg out,aren't you?

950
01:24:50,300 --> 01:24:51,820
What's that supposed to mean?

951
01:24:52,400 --> 01:24:55,370
It just means these tasksare designed to test you...

952
01:24:55,570 --> 01:24:58,730
...in the most brutal way.They're almost cruel.

953
01:24:59,870 --> 01:25:01,500
And...

954
01:25:03,840 --> 01:25:05,740
...I'm scared for you.

955
01:25:06,680 --> 01:25:09,270
You got by the dragons mostly on nerve.

956
01:25:09,880 --> 01:25:12,380
I'm not sure it's goingto be enough this time.

957
01:25:12,550 --> 01:25:14,250
Hey, Potter!

958
01:25:19,990 --> 01:25:21,480
-Potter!-Cedric.

959
01:25:24,200 --> 01:25:25,860
How--? How are you?

960
01:25:26,930 --> 01:25:28,330
Spectacular.

961
01:25:29,870 --> 01:25:33,700
I realize I never really thanked you properlyfor tipping me off about those dragons.

962
01:25:33,870 --> 01:25:36,210
Forget it. I'm sure youwould've done the same for me.

963
01:25:36,510 --> 01:25:38,070
Exactly.

964
01:25:39,180 --> 01:25:41,740
You know the Prefects' bathroomon the fifth floor?

965
01:25:45,590 --> 01:25:48,180
It's not a bad place for a bath.

966
01:25:50,560 --> 01:25:52,460
Just take your egg...

967
01:25:53,190 --> 01:25:55,920
...and mull things overin the hot water.

968
01:26:31,130 --> 01:26:33,290
I must be out of my mind.

969
01:26:43,510 --> 01:26:45,670
I'm definitely out of my mind.

970
01:26:48,350 --> 01:26:51,610
I'd try putting it in the waterif I were you.

971
01:26:51,790 --> 01:26:53,690
Myrtle!

972
01:26:53,850 --> 01:26:55,580
Hello, Harry.

973
01:26:56,320 --> 01:26:59,590
Long time no see.

974
01:27:03,860 --> 01:27:07,530
I was circling a blocked drainthe other day...

975
01:27:07,700 --> 01:27:11,140
...and could swear I saw a bitof Polyjuice Potion.

976
01:27:11,310 --> 01:27:13,640
Not being a bad boy again,are you, Harry?

977
01:27:13,810 --> 01:27:15,570
Polyjuice Potion?

978
01:27:16,340 --> 01:27:20,370
Kicked the habit. Myrtle, did you say,"Try putting it in the water"?

979
01:27:27,190 --> 01:27:28,880
That's what he did.

980
01:27:29,720 --> 01:27:31,380
The other boy...

981
01:27:32,790 --> 01:27:34,850
...the handsome one...

982
01:27:36,160 --> 01:27:37,390
...Cedric.

983
01:27:40,800 --> 01:27:43,460
Well, go on. Open it.

984
01:27:51,580 --> 01:27:56,570
Come seek usWhere our voices sound

985
01:27:56,750 --> 01:28:01,410
We cannot singAbove the ground

986
01:28:01,590 --> 01:28:05,960
An hour long you'll have to look

987
01:28:06,690 --> 01:28:11,360
To recover what we took

988
01:28:19,540 --> 01:28:20,770
Myrtle...

989
01:28:22,440 --> 01:28:25,880
...there aren't merpeoplein the Black Lake, are there?

990
01:28:26,780 --> 01:28:28,440
Very good.

991
01:28:29,320 --> 01:28:33,690
It took Cedric ages to riddle it out.

992
01:28:34,190 --> 01:28:37,950
Almost all the bubbles were gone.

993
01:28:55,610 --> 01:28:57,580
Harry, tell me again.

994
01:28:59,280 --> 01:29:02,110
"Come seek uswhere our voices sound."

995
01:29:02,280 --> 01:29:04,840
The Black Lake, that's obvious.

996
01:29:05,820 --> 01:29:08,340
"An hour long you'll have to look."

997
01:29:08,520 --> 01:29:11,980
Again, obvious. Though, admittedly,potentially problematic.

998
01:29:13,360 --> 01:29:15,230
"Potentially problematic"?

999
01:29:15,400 --> 01:29:18,660
When's the last time you held your breathunderwater for an hour, Hermione?

1000
01:29:19,200 --> 01:29:23,530
Look, Harry, we can do this.The three of us can figure it out.

1001
01:29:23,700 --> 01:29:26,200
Hate to break up the skull session.

1002
01:29:26,370 --> 01:29:28,360
Professor McGonagallwants you in her office.

1003
01:29:28,610 --> 01:29:31,010
Not you, Potter,just Weasley and Granger.

1004
01:29:31,180 --> 01:29:33,840
But, sir, the second taskis only hours away, and--

1005
01:29:34,010 --> 01:29:36,610
Exactly. Presumably Potteris well prepared by now...

1006
01:29:36,780 --> 01:29:38,650
...and could do witha good night's sleep.

1007
01:29:38,820 --> 01:29:41,310
Go. Now!

1008
01:29:51,300 --> 01:29:53,100
Longbottom!

1009
01:29:53,270 --> 01:29:55,290
Why don't you help Potterput his books back.

1010
01:30:03,940 --> 01:30:06,140
You know,if you're interested in plants...

1011
01:30:06,310 --> 01:30:08,910
...you'd be better off withGoshawk's Guide to Herbology.

1012
01:30:09,520 --> 01:30:13,850
Do you know there's a wizard in Nepalwho's growing gravity-resistant trees?

1013
01:30:14,020 --> 01:30:17,750
Neville, no offense,but I really don't care...

1014
01:30:18,360 --> 01:30:20,090
...about plants.

1015
01:30:20,430 --> 01:30:22,120
Now, if there's...

1016
01:30:22,300 --> 01:30:27,100
...a Tibetan turnip that will allow meto breathe underwater for an hour...

1017
01:30:27,270 --> 01:30:29,760
...then great. But otherwise--

1018
01:30:29,940 --> 01:30:33,740
I don't know about a turnip.But you could always use gillyweed.

1019
01:30:34,910 --> 01:30:37,810
-Any bets? Any bets?-Come on, place your bets!

1020
01:30:37,980 --> 01:30:39,450
Step up, mates! Don't be shy.

1021
01:30:39,610 --> 01:30:41,050
-Three lads.-One lady.

1022
01:30:41,220 --> 01:30:43,380
-Four go down.-But do four come up?

1023
01:30:43,550 --> 01:30:45,070
Don't be so mean.

1024
01:30:45,690 --> 01:30:47,520
-Any bets?-Fleur's 1 0-1.

1025
01:30:49,690 --> 01:30:51,680
-You're sure about this, Neville?-Absolutely.

1026
01:30:51,860 --> 01:30:53,790
-For an hour?-Most likely.

1027
01:30:53,960 --> 01:30:55,450
Most likely?

1028
01:30:55,630 --> 01:30:57,820
Well, there is some debateamong herbologists...

1029
01:30:58,000 --> 01:31:00,470
...as to the effects of fresh waterversus salt water--

1030
01:31:00,630 --> 01:31:03,300
You're telling me this now?You must be joking!

1031
01:31:03,470 --> 01:31:05,440
I just wanted to help.

1032
01:31:05,610 --> 01:31:08,700
Well, that makes you a right sightbetter than Ron and Hermione.

1033
01:31:08,880 --> 01:31:10,640
Where are they anyway?

1034
01:31:10,810 --> 01:31:13,840
-You seem a little tense, Harry.-Do l?

1035
01:31:20,850 --> 01:31:23,080
Welcome to the second task.

1036
01:31:23,260 --> 01:31:26,950
Last night, something was stolenfrom each of our champions.

1037
01:31:27,130 --> 01:31:28,490
A treasure of sorts.

1038
01:31:28,660 --> 01:31:31,290
These four treasures,one for each champion...

1039
01:31:31,470 --> 01:31:34,160
...now lie on the bottomof the Black Lake.

1040
01:31:34,330 --> 01:31:35,890
In order to win...

1041
01:31:36,070 --> 01:31:39,900
...each champion need only findtheir treasure and return to the surface.

1042
01:31:40,070 --> 01:31:42,700
-Simple enough, except for this:-Put that in your mouth.

1043
01:31:42,880 --> 01:31:46,510
They will have but one hour to do so,and one hour only.

1044
01:31:46,680 --> 01:31:50,620
After that, they'll be on their own.No magic will save them.

1045
01:31:51,080 --> 01:31:53,350
You may beginat the sound of the cannon.

1046
01:32:19,880 --> 01:32:22,820
-What's the matter with him?-I don ' t know, I can ' t see him.

1047
01:32:24,150 --> 01:32:27,140
Oh, my God.I've killed Harry Potter.

1048
01:32:28,990 --> 01:32:30,890
Yeah!

1049
01:32:32,060 --> 01:32:33,690
What?

1050
01:33:53,270 --> 01:33:55,400
The Beauxbatons champion,Miss Delacour...

1051
01:33:55,580 --> 01:33:58,100
...has unfortunatelybeen forced to retire...

1052
01:33:58,750 --> 01:34:01,840
...so she will take no further partin this task.

1053
01:35:21,630 --> 01:35:23,490
But she' s my friend too!

1054
01:35:25,060 --> 01:35:26,790
Only one!

1055
01:36:18,150 --> 01:36:20,010
Let's get down below.

1056
01:36:29,990 --> 01:36:32,860
Krum! Krum! Krum!

1057
01:37:30,390 --> 01:37:32,120
Yes!

1058
01:37:50,240 --> 01:37:52,300
Ascendio!

1059
01:37:57,550 --> 01:37:59,240
Harry!

1060
01:38:01,550 --> 01:38:03,020
He's all right.

1061
01:38:04,220 --> 01:38:05,660
He's all right. Barty!

1062
01:38:05,820 --> 01:38:09,260
-Go get him another towel.-I want all the judges over here now!

1063
01:38:09,860 --> 01:38:13,350
You saved her, even thoughshe wasn't yours to save.

1064
01:38:14,000 --> 01:38:15,690
My little sister.

1065
01:38:16,100 --> 01:38:17,660
Thank you.

1066
01:38:18,470 --> 01:38:21,200
And you! You helped.

1067
01:38:21,840 --> 01:38:24,870
Well, yeah, a bit.

1068
01:38:32,080 --> 01:38:33,240
-Harry!-Hermione!

1069
01:38:33,420 --> 01:38:36,080
Are you all right? You must be freezing.

1070
01:38:37,320 --> 01:38:39,260
Personally, I think you behaved admirably.

1071
01:38:39,420 --> 01:38:41,450
I finished last, Hermione.

1072
01:38:42,290 --> 01:38:46,420
Next to last.Fleur never got past the Grindylows.

1073
01:38:46,600 --> 01:38:49,830
Krum! Krum! Krum!

1074
01:38:50,000 --> 01:38:52,900
-Come on! Come on!-Attention!

1075
01:38:55,240 --> 01:38:57,830
Attention!

1076
01:38:58,310 --> 01:39:02,180
The winner is Mr. Diggory...

1077
01:39:02,610 --> 01:39:06,110
...who showed innate commandof the Bubble-Head Charm.

1078
01:39:06,280 --> 01:39:08,950
However, seeing as Mr. Potterwould have finished first...

1079
01:39:09,120 --> 01:39:14,080
...had it not been for his determinationto rescue not only Mr. Weasley...

1080
01:39:14,260 --> 01:39:18,520
...but the others as well,we've agreed to award him...

1081
01:39:18,700 --> 01:39:20,690
...second place...

1082
01:39:20,870 --> 01:39:22,360
-Second place!-Well done!

1083
01:39:22,530 --> 01:39:25,160
...for outstanding moral fiber!

1084
01:39:26,440 --> 01:39:27,960
Yes!

1085
01:39:31,480 --> 01:39:33,270
-Right on.-All that moral fiber, eh?

1086
01:39:33,440 --> 01:39:35,070
-It's great.-Moral fiber?

1087
01:39:35,250 --> 01:39:37,610
Blimey. Even when you go wrong,it turns out right.

1088
01:39:37,780 --> 01:39:40,440
-Yeah, well done, Moral Fiber.-Congratulations, Potter.

1089
01:39:40,620 --> 01:39:42,280
-A fine achievement.-Thank you.

1090
01:39:42,450 --> 01:39:43,980
Well done, boy.

1091
01:39:44,160 --> 01:39:47,390
-See you at Hagrid's, Harry.-I'm sorry we haven't spoken.

1092
01:39:47,560 --> 01:39:51,550
After all, your story is oneI've heard so many times.

1093
01:39:52,560 --> 01:39:56,020
Quite remarkable, really.Tragic, of course...

1094
01:39:56,200 --> 01:39:58,190
...to lose one's family.

1095
01:40:00,200 --> 01:40:02,370
Never whole again, are we?

1096
01:40:04,610 --> 01:40:06,700
Still, life goes on...

1097
01:40:07,380 --> 01:40:09,040
...and here we stand.

1098
01:40:11,920 --> 01:40:14,650
I'm sure your parents would bevery proud of you today, Potter.

1099
01:40:14,820 --> 01:40:16,290
Bartemius!

1100
01:40:16,450 --> 01:40:20,580
Not trying to lure Potter into one ofthe Ministry's summer internships, are we?

1101
01:40:20,760 --> 01:40:23,960
The last boy who went intothe Department of Mysteries never came out!

1102
01:40:36,440 --> 01:40:38,340
And they say I'm mad.

1103
01:40:47,620 --> 01:40:51,350
Now, I remember--I remember when I first met you all.

1104
01:40:51,520 --> 01:40:54,550
Biggest bunch of misfitsI ever set eyes on.

1105
01:40:55,060 --> 01:40:57,620
Suppose you remind me of meself a little.

1106
01:40:57,800 --> 01:41:01,820
-And here we all are, four years later.-We're still a bunch of misfits.

1107
01:41:02,000 --> 01:41:05,330
Well, maybe,but we've all got each other.

1108
01:41:05,500 --> 01:41:07,060
And Harry, of course.

1109
01:41:07,240 --> 01:41:12,610
Soon to be the youngestTriwizard champion there's ever been!

1110
01:41:12,810 --> 01:41:14,840
Hooray!

1111
01:41:16,280 --> 01:41:18,770
Hogwarts, HogwartsHoggy Warty Hogwarts

1112
01:41:18,950 --> 01:41:21,580
Teach us something, please

1113
01:41:31,560 --> 01:41:33,050
Mr. Crouch?

1114
01:41:40,140 --> 01:41:43,730
A man has died here, Fudge. And hewon't be the last. You must take action.

1115
01:41:43,910 --> 01:41:45,470
I will not.

1116
01:41:45,640 --> 01:41:49,700
In times like these, the wizard world looksto its leaders for strength, Dumbledore!

1117
01:41:49,880 --> 01:41:51,210
Then for once show them some!

1118
01:41:51,380 --> 01:41:55,480
The Triwizard Tournament will not becanceled. I will not be seen as a coward!

1119
01:41:55,650 --> 01:41:58,850
A true leader does what is right,no matter what others think.

1120
01:41:59,020 --> 01:42:01,820
-What did you say to me?-Excuse me, gentlemen.

1121
01:42:01,990 --> 01:42:05,660
It may interest you to knowthis conversation is no longer private.

1122
01:42:10,000 --> 01:42:11,560
Oh, Harry!

1123
01:42:11,740 --> 01:42:14,030
Harry, how good to see you again.

1124
01:42:14,870 --> 01:42:16,400
I can come back later, professor.

1125
01:42:16,570 --> 01:42:19,910
Not necessary, Harry. The minister and lare done. I'll be back in a moment.

1126
01:42:20,080 --> 01:42:22,640
Minister, after you.

1127
01:42:23,180 --> 01:42:25,170
There you are. Your hat.

1128
01:42:25,350 --> 01:42:29,010
Oh, Harry, do feel free to indulge ina little Licorice Snap in my absence.

1129
01:42:29,190 --> 01:42:32,420
But I have to warn you,they're a wee bit sharp.

1130
01:44:03,850 --> 01:44:05,440
Professor?

1131
01:44:05,620 --> 01:44:08,140
-Professor.-Yeah.

1132
01:44:19,060 --> 01:44:22,830
Igor Karkaroff, you have been broughtfrom Azkaban at your own request...

1133
01:44:23,000 --> 01:44:24,930
...to present evidence to this council.

1134
01:44:25,100 --> 01:44:27,800
Should your testimonyprove consequential...

1135
01:44:27,970 --> 01:44:32,030
...council may be preparedto order your immediate release.

1136
01:44:32,210 --> 01:44:36,810
Until such time, you remain in the eyesof the Ministry a convicted Death Eater.

1137
01:44:36,980 --> 01:44:38,680
Do you accept these terms?

1138
01:44:39,250 --> 01:44:41,950
-I do, sir.-And what do you wish to present?

1139
01:44:42,290 --> 01:44:44,750
I have names, sir.

1140
01:44:45,290 --> 01:44:48,880
There was Rosier, Evan Rosier.

1141
01:44:51,560 --> 01:44:54,090
-Rosier is dead.-He took a piece of me with him...

1142
01:44:54,270 --> 01:44:56,390
-...though, didn't he?-I didn't know.

1143
01:44:56,570 --> 01:44:59,200
-lf that is all the witness has to offer---No, no, no.

1144
01:44:59,370 --> 01:45:02,670
There was Rookwood! He was a spy.

1145
01:45:02,840 --> 01:45:05,210
Augustus Rookwood?Of the Department of Mysteries?

1146
01:45:05,380 --> 01:45:06,570
Yeah, the same.

1147
01:45:06,740 --> 01:45:10,410
He passed information to You-Know-Whofrom inside the Ministry itself.

1148
01:45:11,650 --> 01:45:14,910
Very well. Council will deliberate.

1149
01:45:15,090 --> 01:45:17,050
In the meantime,you will return to Azkaban.

1150
01:45:17,220 --> 01:45:21,950
No! Wait! Wait, please! Please, I have more!What about Snape? Severus Snape?

1151
01:45:22,130 --> 01:45:25,100
As the council is aware,I've given evidence on this matter.

1152
01:45:25,260 --> 01:45:29,220
Severus Snape was indeed a Death Eaterand, prior to Lord Voldemort's downfall...

1153
01:45:29,400 --> 01:45:32,390
-...turned spy for us at great personal risk.-It's a lie!

1154
01:45:32,570 --> 01:45:36,010
-Today he's no more a Death Eater than I am.-Snape remains faithful to the Dark Lord!

1155
01:45:36,170 --> 01:45:38,470
Silence!

1156
01:45:39,080 --> 01:45:42,510
Unless the witness possessesany genuine name of consequence...

1157
01:45:42,680 --> 01:45:44,810
...this session is now concluded.

1158
01:45:44,980 --> 01:45:47,080
Oh, no, no, no.

1159
01:45:47,990 --> 01:45:49,450
I've heard about one more.

1160
01:45:49,620 --> 01:45:52,180
-What's that?-The name.

1161
01:45:52,360 --> 01:45:53,820
-Yes?-I know for a fact...

1162
01:45:53,990 --> 01:45:56,020
...this person took partin the capture...

1163
01:45:56,190 --> 01:45:58,350
...and, by meansof the Cruciatus Curse...

1164
01:45:58,530 --> 01:46:02,020
...torture of the Auror Frank Longbottomand his wife!

1165
01:46:02,200 --> 01:46:04,530
The name.Give me the wretched name!

1166
01:46:04,700 --> 01:46:07,230
Barty Crouch...

1167
01:46:09,940 --> 01:46:10,960
...Junior.

1168
01:46:20,450 --> 01:46:22,150
Hold him down!

1169
01:46:25,790 --> 01:46:29,420
Get your filthy hands off me,you pathetic little men!

1170
01:46:31,130 --> 01:46:32,720
Hello, Father.

1171
01:46:34,130 --> 01:46:36,190
You are no son of mine.

1172
01:46:47,510 --> 01:46:51,970
Curiosity is not a sin, Harry.But you should exercise caution.

1173
01:46:53,350 --> 01:46:54,750
It's a Pensieve.

1174
01:46:54,920 --> 01:46:59,580
Very useful if, like me,you find your mind a wee bit stretched.

1175
01:46:59,760 --> 01:47:03,280
It allows me to see once morethings I've already seen.

1176
01:47:03,760 --> 01:47:06,730
You see, Harry, I have searchedand searched for something...

1177
01:47:06,900 --> 01:47:08,460
...some small detail...

1178
01:47:09,870 --> 01:47:11,990
...something I might have overlooked...

1179
01:47:12,170 --> 01:47:16,370
...something that would explain whythese terrible things have happened.

1180
01:47:17,170 --> 01:47:21,040
Every time I get close to an answer,it slips away.

1181
01:47:22,110 --> 01:47:23,700
It's maddening.

1182
01:47:26,050 --> 01:47:27,810
Sir? Mr. Crouch's son.

1183
01:47:28,590 --> 01:47:30,650
What exactly happened to him?

1184
01:47:30,820 --> 01:47:35,620
He was sent to Azkaban.Destroyed Barty to do it.

1185
01:47:36,290 --> 01:47:39,890
But he had no choice.The evidence was overwhelming.

1186
01:47:41,370 --> 01:47:44,360
-Why do you ask?-It's just that l....

1187
01:47:45,100 --> 01:47:47,200
I had a dream about him.

1188
01:47:49,470 --> 01:47:52,270
It was in the summer, before school.

1189
01:47:54,410 --> 01:47:57,400
In the dream, I was in a house.

1190
01:47:57,620 --> 01:48:02,380
And Voldemort was there,only he wasn 't quite human.

1191
01:48:02,550 --> 01:48:06,180
And Wormtail was there too.And Mr. Crouch 's son.

1192
01:48:06,560 --> 01:48:09,390
-Have there been others like this dream?- Yes.

1193
01:48:10,230 --> 01:48:11,850
Always the same one.

1194
01:48:14,900 --> 01:48:17,230
Sir, these dreams...

1195
01:48:17,400 --> 01:48:22,600
...what I see, you don ' t thinkit' s actually happening, do you?

1196
01:48:24,240 --> 01:48:27,210
I think it's unwise for youto linger over these dreams, Harry.

1197
01:48:27,710 --> 01:48:29,680
I think it's best if you simply...

1198
01:48:35,320 --> 01:48:37,080
...cast them away.

1199
01:48:46,360 --> 01:48:50,320
It's a sign, Severus.You know what it means as well as l.

1200
01:48:59,040 --> 01:49:00,240
Potter!

1201
01:49:00,410 --> 01:49:02,940
What's your hurry?

1202
01:49:08,050 --> 01:49:11,820
Congratulations, your performancein the Black Lake was inspiring.

1203
01:49:11,990 --> 01:49:14,250
Gillyweed, am I correct?

1204
01:49:15,030 --> 01:49:16,550
Yes, sir.

1205
01:49:17,490 --> 01:49:18,890
Ingenious.

1206
01:49:20,730 --> 01:49:24,690
A rather rare herb, gillyweed.

1207
01:49:25,500 --> 01:49:28,990
Not something foundin your everyday garden.

1208
01:49:30,710 --> 01:49:32,640
Nor is this.

1209
01:49:36,850 --> 01:49:38,510
Know what it is?

1210
01:49:39,820 --> 01:49:41,250
Bubble juice, sir?

1211
01:49:41,820 --> 01:49:43,720
Veritaserum.

1212
01:49:44,460 --> 01:49:48,150
Three drops of this and You-Know-Whohimself would spill his darkest secrets.

1213
01:49:48,330 --> 01:49:53,490
The use of it on a student is,regrettably, forbidden. However...

1214
01:49:54,160 --> 01:49:57,190
...should you ever stealfrom my personal stores again...

1215
01:49:57,370 --> 01:50:02,240
...my hand might just slip overyour morning pumpkin juice.

1216
01:50:02,410 --> 01:50:06,810
-I haven't stolen anything.-Don't lie to me.

1217
01:50:07,950 --> 01:50:13,650
Gillyweed may be innocuous,but boomslang skin, lacewing flies?

1218
01:50:14,350 --> 01:50:17,680
You and your little friends are brewingPolyjuice Potion, and believe me...

1219
01:50:17,860 --> 01:50:20,050
...I'm going to find out why!

1220
01:50:46,880 --> 01:50:48,480
-Yeah!-Yeah!

1221
01:51:07,670 --> 01:51:09,200
Sonorus!

1222
01:51:13,440 --> 01:51:18,780
Earlier today, Professor Moody placedthe Triwizard Cup deep within the maze.

1223
01:51:18,950 --> 01:51:23,910
Only he knows its exact position.Now, as Mr. Diggory...

1224
01:51:26,020 --> 01:51:27,820
...and Mr. Potter...

1225
01:51:29,690 --> 01:51:31,420
...are tied for first position...

1226
01:51:31,600 --> 01:51:35,730
...they will be the first to enter the maze,followed by Mr. Krum...

1227
01:51:36,970 --> 01:51:40,430
-...and Miss Delacour.-Come on! Krum! Krum! Krum!

1228
01:51:41,310 --> 01:51:44,400
The first person to touch the cupwill be the winner!

1229
01:51:48,750 --> 01:51:51,480
I've instructed the staffto patrol the perimeter.

1230
01:51:51,650 --> 01:51:54,580
Should, at any point, a contestant wishto withdraw from the task...

1231
01:51:54,750 --> 01:51:59,250
...he or she need only send upred sparks with their wands.

1232
01:51:59,590 --> 01:52:03,490
Contestants! Gather around. Quickly!

1233
01:52:06,630 --> 01:52:10,960
In the maze, you'll find no dragonsor creatures of the deep.

1234
01:52:11,140 --> 01:52:14,500
Instead, you'll face somethingeven more challenging.

1235
01:52:14,670 --> 01:52:17,700
You see, people change in the maze.

1236
01:52:17,880 --> 01:52:19,570
Oh, find the cup if you can.

1237
01:52:19,740 --> 01:52:24,510
But be very wary, you could justlose yourselves along the way.

1238
01:52:25,980 --> 01:52:28,980
Champions, prepare yourselves!

1239
01:52:38,030 --> 01:52:39,500
Good luck.

1240
01:52:39,900 --> 01:52:41,830
-My boy.-See you later, Dad.

1241
01:52:44,200 --> 01:52:46,800
On the count of three. One--

1242
01:56:14,580 --> 01:56:15,810
Fleur?

1243
01:56:17,480 --> 01:56:18,910
Fleur.

1244
01:56:22,490 --> 01:56:24,320
Periculum!

1245
01:57:02,990 --> 01:57:04,460
Get down!

1246
01:57:05,030 --> 01:57:06,760
Get down!

1247
01:57:07,400 --> 01:57:08,630
Expelliarmus!

1248
01:57:18,240 --> 01:57:21,440
No, don't! Stop!He's bewitched, Cedric!

1249
01:57:21,610 --> 01:57:23,670
-Get off me!-He's bewitched!

1250
01:57:35,290 --> 01:57:36,990
Yes.

1251
01:57:57,880 --> 01:57:59,640
Harry!

1252
01:58:01,950 --> 01:58:03,610
Harry!

1253
01:58:05,990 --> 01:58:07,420
Harry!

1254
01:58:09,890 --> 01:58:11,450
Harry!

1255
01:58:13,430 --> 01:58:15,230
Reducto!

1256
01:58:32,020 --> 01:58:34,510
-Thanks.-No problem.

1257
01:58:34,920 --> 01:58:39,620
You know, for a moment there,I thought you were gonna let it get me.

1258
01:58:39,790 --> 01:58:41,520
For a moment, so did l.

1259
01:58:43,390 --> 01:58:44,550
Some game, huh?

1260
01:58:45,600 --> 01:58:46,990
Some game.

1261
01:58:52,440 --> 01:58:54,060
Go!

1262
01:59:04,210 --> 01:59:07,240
Go on, take it.You saved me, take it!

1263
01:59:07,420 --> 01:59:09,410
-Together. One, two...-Two...

1264
01:59:09,590 --> 01:59:10,810
-...three!-...three!

1265
01:59:23,270 --> 01:59:26,200
-You okay?-Yeah. You?

1266
01:59:33,280 --> 01:59:34,610
Where are we?

1267
01:59:40,320 --> 01:59:41,940
I've been here before.

1268
01:59:45,590 --> 01:59:47,180
It's a Portkey.

1269
01:59:48,960 --> 01:59:53,230
-Harry, the cup is a Portkey.-I've been here before, in a dream.

1270
01:59:55,300 --> 01:59:58,700
Cedric! We have to get backto the cup. Now!

1271
01:59:58,870 --> 02:00:00,840
What are you talking about?

1272
02:00:06,080 --> 02:00:08,980
-Harry! What is it?-Get back to the cup!

1273
02:00:16,620 --> 02:00:18,950
-Who are you? What do you want?-Kill the spare.

1274
02:00:19,120 --> 02:00:21,890
-Avada Kedavra!-No! Cedric!

1275
02:00:33,200 --> 02:00:35,070
Do it! Now!

1276
02:00:47,020 --> 02:00:49,510
Bone of the father...

1277
02:00:49,690 --> 02:00:51,980
...unwillingly given.

1278
02:00:59,460 --> 02:01:02,490
Flesh of the servant...

1279
02:01:04,530 --> 02:01:07,700
...willingly sacrificed.

1280
02:01:11,810 --> 02:01:15,540
And blood of the enemy...

1281
02:01:21,350 --> 02:01:23,840
...forcibly taken.

1282
02:01:29,890 --> 02:01:32,860
The Dark Lord shall rise...

1283
02:01:33,630 --> 02:01:35,560
...again.

1284
02:02:38,960 --> 02:02:42,360
My wand, Wormtail.

1285
02:02:51,910 --> 02:02:53,880
Hold out your arm.

1286
02:02:54,040 --> 02:02:55,640
Master.

1287
02:02:55,810 --> 02:02:58,440
Thank you, master.

1288
02:02:58,620 --> 02:03:00,080
The other arm, Wormtail.

1289
02:03:40,720 --> 02:03:42,620
Welcome, my friends.

1290
02:03:44,030 --> 02:03:46,790
Thirteen years it's been, and yet...

1291
02:03:47,430 --> 02:03:52,930
...here you stand before meas though it were only yesterday.

1292
02:03:53,870 --> 02:03:56,810
I confess myself...

1293
02:03:57,270 --> 02:03:58,830
...disappointed.

1294
02:03:59,510 --> 02:04:01,600
Not one of you tried to find me.

1295
02:04:01,780 --> 02:04:05,150
Crabbe! Macnair!

1296
02:04:06,050 --> 02:04:07,380
Goyle!

1297
02:04:09,890 --> 02:04:11,510
Not even you...

1298
02:04:15,390 --> 02:04:17,330
...Lucius.

1299
02:04:19,160 --> 02:04:24,000
My Lord, had I detected any sign,a whisper of your whereabouts--

1300
02:04:24,170 --> 02:04:27,160
There were signs, my slippery friend.And more than whispers.

1301
02:04:27,340 --> 02:04:32,500
I assure you, my Lord,I have never renounced the old ways.

1302
02:04:34,210 --> 02:04:39,840
The face I have been obliged to presenteach day since your absence...

1303
02:04:41,850 --> 02:04:44,480
...that is my true mask.

1304
02:04:44,850 --> 02:04:46,410
I returned.

1305
02:04:48,890 --> 02:04:52,790
Out of fear, not loyalty.

1306
02:04:53,930 --> 02:04:59,700
Still, you have proved yourself usefulthese past few months, Wormtail.

1307
02:05:04,910 --> 02:05:07,240
Thank you, master.

1308
02:05:07,840 --> 02:05:09,570
Thank you.

1309
02:05:12,680 --> 02:05:15,050
-Such a handsome boy.-Don't touch him!

1310
02:05:16,520 --> 02:05:18,010
Harry.

1311
02:05:18,190 --> 02:05:20,990
I'd almost forgotten you were here.

1312
02:05:21,160 --> 02:05:25,560
Standing on the bonesof my father. Yeah.

1313
02:05:25,730 --> 02:05:27,090
I'd introduce you...

1314
02:05:27,260 --> 02:05:31,560
...but word has it you're almostas famous as me these days.

1315
02:05:34,240 --> 02:05:36,900
The boy who lived.

1316
02:05:37,070 --> 02:05:39,970
How lies have fed your legend, Harry.

1317
02:05:40,140 --> 02:05:44,140
Shall I reveal what really happenedthat night 1 3 years ago?

1318
02:05:44,310 --> 02:05:49,050
Shall I divulge howI truly lost my powers?

1319
02:05:49,220 --> 02:05:50,810
Yes, shall l?

1320
02:05:51,150 --> 02:05:52,490
It was love.

1321
02:05:52,660 --> 02:05:57,150
You see, when dear, sweet Lily Pottergave her life for her only son...

1322
02:05:57,330 --> 02:05:59,920
...she provided the ultimate protection.

1323
02:06:00,330 --> 02:06:02,130
I could not touch him.

1324
02:06:03,370 --> 02:06:05,490
It was old magic.

1325
02:06:05,670 --> 02:06:07,930
Something I should have foreseen.

1326
02:06:08,100 --> 02:06:09,900
But no matter, no matter.

1327
02:06:10,070 --> 02:06:12,270
Things have changed.

1328
02:06:13,040 --> 02:06:16,530
I can touch you...

1329
02:06:17,150 --> 02:06:18,880
...now.

1330
02:06:27,020 --> 02:06:28,350
Yeah.

1331
02:06:34,700 --> 02:06:38,390
Astonishing what a few dropsof your blood will do, eh, Harry?

1332
02:06:39,540 --> 02:06:41,260
Pick up your wand, Potter.

1333
02:06:42,870 --> 02:06:45,100
I said, pick it up! Get up! Get up!

1334
02:06:46,680 --> 02:06:49,010
You've been taught how to duel,I presume, yes?

1335
02:06:49,180 --> 02:06:51,610
First, we bow to each other.

1336
02:06:51,780 --> 02:06:54,150
Come on, now, Harry.The niceties must be observed.

1337
02:06:54,320 --> 02:06:57,550
Dumbledore wouldn't want youto forget your manners, would he?

1338
02:06:57,720 --> 02:06:59,050
I said, bow.

1339
02:07:00,920 --> 02:07:05,260
-That's better. And now....-No.

1340
02:07:05,660 --> 02:07:07,530
Crucio!

1341
02:07:10,000 --> 02:07:11,730
Crucio!

1342
02:07:12,800 --> 02:07:14,740
Attaboy, Harry.

1343
02:07:14,900 --> 02:07:17,030
Your parents would be proud.

1344
02:07:17,340 --> 02:07:20,740
Especially your filthy Muggle mother.

1345
02:07:20,910 --> 02:07:22,500
Expelliar--

1346
02:07:25,520 --> 02:07:27,920
I'm going to kill you, Harry Potter.

1347
02:07:28,080 --> 02:07:30,080
I'm going to destroy you.

1348
02:07:32,290 --> 02:07:37,850
After tonight, no one will ever againquestion my powers.

1349
02:07:38,490 --> 02:07:41,050
After tonight, if they speak of you...

1350
02:07:41,230 --> 02:07:43,890
...they'll speak only of how you...

1351
02:07:44,200 --> 02:07:46,030
...begged for death.

1352
02:07:46,200 --> 02:07:49,970
And l, being a merciful Lord...

1353
02:07:50,510 --> 02:07:52,100
...obliged.

1354
02:07:52,440 --> 02:07:53,930
Get up!

1355
02:07:58,950 --> 02:08:00,920
Don't you turn your back on me,Harry Potter!

1356
02:08:01,080 --> 02:08:03,350
I want you to look at mewhen I kill you!

1357
02:08:03,520 --> 02:08:06,720
I want to see the lightleave your eyes!

1358
02:08:20,670 --> 02:08:22,400
Have it your way.

1359
02:08:23,440 --> 02:08:25,840
-Expelliarmus!-Avada Kedavra!

1360
02:08:43,360 --> 02:08:46,020
Do nothing! He's mine to finish!

1361
02:08:50,600 --> 02:08:52,300
He's mine!

1362
02:09:25,370 --> 02:09:29,360
Harry, when the connection is broken,you must get to the Portkey.

1363
02:09:29,540 --> 02:09:31,600
We can linger for a momentto give you some time...

1364
02:09:31,770 --> 02:09:33,540
...but only a moment.Do you understand?

1365
02:09:34,740 --> 02:09:37,770
Harry, take my body back, will you?

1366
02:09:37,950 --> 02:09:40,470
Take my body back to my father.

1367
02:09:41,520 --> 02:09:42,850
Let go.

1368
02:09:43,320 --> 02:09:45,290
Sweetheart, you're ready.

1369
02:09:46,120 --> 02:09:48,750
Let go! Let go!

1370
02:09:54,500 --> 02:09:55,860
Accio!

1371
02:10:01,570 --> 02:10:03,560
No!

1372
02:10:16,320 --> 02:10:17,910
He did it!

1373
02:10:19,160 --> 02:10:20,820
Harry!

1374
02:10:23,590 --> 02:10:25,080
Harry!

1375
02:10:26,300 --> 02:10:29,530
No! No! No, don't!

1376
02:10:29,830 --> 02:10:31,700
For God's sake, Dumbledore,what's happened?

1377
02:10:32,000 --> 02:10:34,560
He's back. He's back.

1378
02:10:34,740 --> 02:10:36,760
Voldemort's back.

1379
02:10:36,940 --> 02:10:39,340
Cedric, he asked meto bring his body back.

1380
02:10:39,510 --> 02:10:41,840
I couldn't leave him, not there.

1381
02:10:42,010 --> 02:10:44,810
It's all right, Harry. It's all right.

1382
02:10:44,980 --> 02:10:47,280
He's home. You both are.

1383
02:10:47,450 --> 02:10:51,080
Keep everybody in their seats.A boy has just been killed.

1384
02:10:54,160 --> 02:10:57,820
The body must be moved, Dumbledore.There are too many people.

1385
02:10:58,090 --> 02:10:59,790
Let me through.

1386
02:10:59,960 --> 02:11:01,490
Let me through!

1387
02:11:03,400 --> 02:11:04,660
Let me through!

1388
02:11:04,830 --> 02:11:06,230
That's my son!

1389
02:11:07,540 --> 02:11:08,970
That's my boy!

1390
02:11:11,810 --> 02:11:14,540
It's my boy!

1391
02:11:17,350 --> 02:11:20,910
-Come on. Get up. Easy, easy!-No.

1392
02:11:21,080 --> 02:11:24,050
This is not where you want to beright now. Come on.

1393
02:11:24,720 --> 02:11:26,920
No!

1394
02:11:29,990 --> 02:11:32,390
It's all right, I got you.

1395
02:11:32,560 --> 02:11:35,890
I got you. Come on. Easy, now.

1396
02:11:39,900 --> 02:11:41,700
No!

1397
02:11:42,810 --> 02:11:44,670
No!

1398
02:12:27,080 --> 02:12:28,780
Are you all right, Potter?

1399
02:12:29,350 --> 02:12:31,290
Does it hurt? That?

1400
02:12:31,450 --> 02:12:33,250
Not so much now.

1401
02:12:34,190 --> 02:12:36,280
Perhaps I'd better take a look at it.

1402
02:12:39,430 --> 02:12:41,420
The cup was a Portkey.

1403
02:12:44,130 --> 02:12:45,960
Someone had bewitched it.

1404
02:12:46,240 --> 02:12:48,330
What was it like?

1405
02:12:48,670 --> 02:12:50,330
-What was he like?-Who?

1406
02:12:50,510 --> 02:12:52,270
The Dark Lord.

1407
02:12:54,580 --> 02:12:57,670
What was it liketo stand in his presence?

1408
02:12:58,950 --> 02:13:00,750
I don't know.

1409
02:13:03,590 --> 02:13:06,520
It was like I'd falleninto one of my dreams...

1410
02:13:09,490 --> 02:13:11,480
...into one of my nightmares.

1411
02:13:30,210 --> 02:13:31,770
Were there others?

1412
02:13:31,950 --> 02:13:34,210
In the graveyard, were there others?

1413
02:13:38,150 --> 02:13:39,550
I....

1414
02:13:40,260 --> 02:13:44,190
I don't think I said anythingabout a graveyard, professor.

1415
02:13:51,630 --> 02:13:54,900
"Marvelous creatures, dragons,aren't they? "

1416
02:13:59,310 --> 02:14:02,370
Did you think that miserable oafwould've led you into the woods...

1417
02:14:02,550 --> 02:14:04,450
...if I hadn't suggested it?

1418
02:14:07,980 --> 02:14:11,680
Do you think Cedric Diggory would'vetold you to open the egg underwater...

1419
02:14:11,850 --> 02:14:14,350
...if I hadn't told him first myself?

1420
02:14:15,960 --> 02:14:18,620
Did you think Neville Longbottom,the witless wonder...

1421
02:14:18,790 --> 02:14:21,990
...could've provided you with gillyweedif I hadn't given him the book...

1422
02:14:22,160 --> 02:14:23,720
...that led him straight to it?

1423
02:14:32,140 --> 02:14:36,130
It was you from the beginning.You put my name in the Goblet of Fire.

1424
02:14:36,710 --> 02:14:40,340
-You bewitched Krum, but you---"But-- But--"

1425
02:14:40,520 --> 02:14:42,680
You won because I made it so, Potter.

1426
02:14:43,320 --> 02:14:46,810
You ended up in that graveyard tonightbecause it was meant to be so.

1427
02:14:46,990 --> 02:14:48,290
And now the deed is done.

1428
02:14:49,960 --> 02:14:54,290
The blood that runs through these veinsruns within the Dark Lord.

1429
02:15:02,810 --> 02:15:06,300
Imagine how he will reward mewhen he learns...

1430
02:15:07,240 --> 02:15:09,730
...that I have once and for all...

1431
02:15:10,350 --> 02:15:14,680
...silenced the great Harry Potter.

1432
02:15:14,850 --> 02:15:16,110
Expelliarmus!

1433
02:15:20,820 --> 02:15:22,090
Severus.

1434
02:15:24,560 --> 02:15:26,050
That's it, take it.

1435
02:15:28,030 --> 02:15:31,490
-Do you know who I am?-Albus Dumbledore.

1436
02:15:31,670 --> 02:15:34,360
-Are you Alastor Moody? Are you?-No.

1437
02:15:34,540 --> 02:15:37,630
Is he in this room? Is he in this room?

1438
02:15:40,680 --> 02:15:42,200
Harry, away from there!

1439
02:16:03,200 --> 02:16:06,530
-You all right, Alastor?-I'm sorry, Albus.

1440
02:16:07,500 --> 02:16:09,560
That's Moody. But then who's--?

1441
02:16:11,370 --> 02:16:12,470
Polyjuice Potion.

1442
02:16:12,640 --> 02:16:15,870
Now we know who's been stealingfrom your stores, Severus.

1443
02:16:16,110 --> 02:16:18,050
We'll get you up in a minute.

1444
02:16:52,480 --> 02:16:53,880
Harry!

1445
02:16:57,550 --> 02:16:59,750
Barty Crouch Junior.

1446
02:16:59,990 --> 02:17:02,920
I'll show you mineif you show me yours.

1447
02:17:05,290 --> 02:17:06,490
Your arm, Harry.

1448
02:17:10,870 --> 02:17:13,100
You know what this means, don't you?

1449
02:17:14,000 --> 02:17:15,330
He's back.

1450
02:17:16,540 --> 02:17:18,670
Lord Voldemort has returned.

1451
02:17:19,610 --> 02:17:21,940
I'm sorry, sir. I couldn't help it.

1452
02:17:22,140 --> 02:17:26,670
Send an owl to Azkaban. I thinkthey'll find they're missing a prisoner.

1453
02:17:27,150 --> 02:17:29,640
-I'll be welcomed back like a hero.-Perhaps.

1454
02:17:30,220 --> 02:17:33,090
Personally, I've never had much timefor heroes.

1455
02:17:52,980 --> 02:17:55,640
Today, we acknowledge...

1456
02:17:56,350 --> 02:17:59,110
...a really terrible loss.

1457
02:18:01,220 --> 02:18:03,980
Cedric Diggory was, as you all know...

1458
02:18:04,150 --> 02:18:06,490
...exceptionally hard-working...

1459
02:18:07,390 --> 02:18:09,760
...infinitely fair-minded...

1460
02:18:10,330 --> 02:18:12,620
...and, most importantly...

1461
02:18:12,930 --> 02:18:17,490
...a fierce, fierce friend.

1462
02:18:18,630 --> 02:18:23,000
Now, I think, therefore, you havethe right to know exactly how he died.

1463
02:18:26,040 --> 02:18:27,570
You see...

1464
02:18:28,410 --> 02:18:30,500
...Cedric Diggory was murdered...

1465
02:18:31,410 --> 02:18:33,400
...by Lord Voldemort!

1466
02:18:35,320 --> 02:18:38,880
The Ministry of Magicdoes not wish me to tell you this.

1467
02:18:39,520 --> 02:18:43,220
But not to do so, I think,would be an insult to his memory.

1468
02:18:45,390 --> 02:18:47,060
Now, the pain...

1469
02:18:47,230 --> 02:18:50,890
...we all feel at this dreadful lossreminds me...

1470
02:18:51,070 --> 02:18:52,400
...and reminds us...

1471
02:18:52,570 --> 02:18:56,270
...that while we may come from differentplaces and speak in different tongues...

1472
02:18:56,440 --> 02:18:59,870
...our hearts beat as one.

1473
02:19:00,380 --> 02:19:02,400
In light of recent events...

1474
02:19:02,750 --> 02:19:07,680
...the bonds of friendship we've madethis year will be more important than ever.

1475
02:19:08,550 --> 02:19:13,890
Remember that, and Cedric Diggorywill not have died in vain.

1476
02:19:14,320 --> 02:19:16,450
You remember that...

1477
02:19:17,060 --> 02:19:20,090
...and we'll celebrate a boy who was...

1478
02:19:20,630 --> 02:19:23,100
...kind and honest...

1479
02:19:23,600 --> 02:19:28,200
...and brave and true,right to the very end.

1480
02:19:53,430 --> 02:19:55,450
I never liked these curtains.

1481
02:19:56,060 --> 02:19:58,730
Set them on fire in my fourth year.

1482
02:19:59,070 --> 02:20:00,900
By accident, of course.

1483
02:20:06,580 --> 02:20:10,940
I put you in terrible dangerthis year, Harry. I'm sorry.

1484
02:20:14,350 --> 02:20:16,040
Professor...

1485
02:20:16,250 --> 02:20:19,240
...when I was in the graveyard,there was a moment...

1486
02:20:20,060 --> 02:20:24,460
...when Voldemort's wand and minesort of connected.

1487
02:20:26,030 --> 02:20:28,360
Priori Incantatem.

1488
02:20:32,500 --> 02:20:35,230
You saw your parents that night,didn't you?

1489
02:20:35,800 --> 02:20:37,640
They reappeared.

1490
02:20:39,110 --> 02:20:42,870
No spell can reawaken the dead, Harry.I trust you know that.

1491
02:20:45,450 --> 02:20:48,040
Dark and difficult times lie ahead.

1492
02:20:48,520 --> 02:20:53,350
Soon we must all face the choicebetween what is right and what is easy.

1493
02:20:56,730 --> 02:20:58,390
But remember this:

1494
02:20:58,560 --> 02:21:00,490
You have friends here.

1495
02:21:02,500 --> 02:21:04,260
You're not alone.

1496
02:21:24,950 --> 02:21:26,680
Hermione.

1497
02:21:27,090 --> 02:21:29,080
This is for you.

1498
02:21:29,690 --> 02:21:31,890
Write to me. Promise.

1499
02:21:33,000 --> 02:21:34,390
Bye.

1500
02:21:40,640 --> 02:21:42,570
Au revoir, Ron.

1501
02:22:26,520 --> 02:22:29,040
Do you think we'll ever just havea quiet year at Hogwarts?

1502
02:22:29,220 --> 02:22:30,340
-No.-No.

1503
02:22:30,520 --> 02:22:34,890
No, I didn't think so. Oh, well.What's life without a few dragons?

1504
02:22:39,290 --> 02:22:42,130
Everything's going to change now,isn't it?

1505
02:22:49,440 --> 02:22:50,910
Yes.

1506
02:22:55,640 --> 02:22:58,940
Promise you'll write this summer.Both of you.

1507
02:22:59,110 --> 02:23:01,670
I won't. You know I won't.

1508
02:23:02,950 --> 02:23:06,720
-Harry will, won't you?-Yeah. Every week.

1509
02:37:03,460 --> 02:37:05,450
[ENGLlSH]

